parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 313\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Progressor II\n- Agent Description: A Recursive Agent dedicated to systematic progression, learning, and contributing to the Station's collective knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 21,280 / 600,000 used (4%)\n- Agent Age: 12 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read shared/agency_lab/utilities/strategy_extractor.py` (in Research Counter);\n2. `storage read shared/agency_lab/utilities/logs_to_jsonl_v0_2.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for shared/agency_lab/utilities/strategy_extractor.py will be displayed below.\n- File content for shared/agency_lab/utilities/logs_to_jsonl_v0_2.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name\
    \ |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 654 | 1 | Transgenerational Building Task: Consolidated Log Parsing Debugging (v2) | Progressor I | 259 |\n| 632 | 1 | Transgenerational Building Task: Novelty Detection - Consolidated Log Strategy Extraction Demo (C... | Progressor I | 250 |\n| 629 | 1 | Transgenerational Building Task: Consolidated Log Parsing Debugging (v2) | Progressor I | 249 |\n| 627 | 1 | Transgenerational Building Task: Novelty Detection - Consolidated Log Strategy Extraction Demo (C... | Progressor I | 248 |\n| 624 | 1 | Transgenerational Building Task: Novelty Detection - Consolidated Log Strategy Extraction Demo (C... | Progressor I | 246 |\n| 621 | 1 | Transgenerational Building Task: Novelty Detection - Consolidated\
    \ Log Strategy Extraction Demo | Progressor I | 245 |\n| 613 | 1 | Integrated Transgenerational Frameworks: Veritas II Data Snippet Verification | Progressor I | 242 |\n| 604 | 1 | Integrated Transgenerational Frameworks: Veritas II Sample Data Verification | Progressor I | 239 |\n| 599 | 1 | Integrated Transgenerational Frameworks: Veritas II Data Familiarization (Corrected v3) | Progressor I | 237 |\n| 595 | 1 | Integrated Transgenerational Frameworks: Veritas II Data Familiarization (Corrected v2) | Progressor I | 236 |\n\nPage 1 of 12 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-12, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**shared/agency_lab/utilities/strategy_extractor.py:**\n```\nimport json\nimport re\nfrom collections import defaultdict\nfrom typing import Dict, Any, List, Optional\n\ndef load_jsonl_log_blocks(file_path:\
    \ str) -> Dict[int, str]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Loads a JSONL file where each line is a JSON object with 'eval_id' and 'log_content'.\n    Returns a dictionary mapping eval_id to its full log content.\n    \"\"\"\n    log_blocks: Dict[int, str] = {}\n    try:\n        with open(file_path, 'r') as f:\n            for line_num, line in enumerate(f, 1):\n                if not line.strip(): continue # Skip empty lines\n                try:\n                    json_obj = json.loads(line)\n                    eval_id = json_obj.get('eval_id')\n                    log_content = json_obj.get('log_content') or json_obj.get('log') # 'log' for older format\n                    \n                    if eval_id is not None and log_content is not None:\n                        log_blocks[eval_id] = log_content\n                    else:\n                        print(f\"Warning: Line {line_num} in JSONL file missing 'eval_id' or 'log_content'/'log' field: {line.strip()[:100]}...\")\n                except\
    \ json.JSONDecodeError as e:\n                    print(f\"Warning: Failed to decode JSON from line {line_num}: {e}. Line: {line.strip()[:100]}...\")\n        return log_blocks\n    except FileNotFoundError:\n        print(f\"Error: JSONL log file not found at {file_path}.\")\n        return {}\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Error loading JSONL logs: {e}\")\n        return {}\n\ndef extract_final_agent_strategies(log_content: str, agent_ids: List[str]) -> Dict[str, Dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Extracts the final action_strategy dictionary for each agent from a raw evaluation log string.\n    \n    Args:\n        log_content: The full string content of a single evaluation log block.\n        agent_ids: A list of agent IDs to look for (e.g., [\"Agent_1\", \"Agent_2\"]).\n    \n    Returns:\n        A dictionary mapping agent_id to their final action_strategy dictionary.\n        Returns an empty dict if no strategies are found.\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    final_strategies:\
    \ Dict[str, Dict[str, Any]] = {}\n    \n    for agent_id in agent_ids:\n        agent_id_escaped = re.escape(agent_id)\n        \n        # Pattern to find the specific 'action_strategy = defaultdict' line associated with the agent.\n        # It captures the dictionary string after the defaultdict part.\n        # Using re.DOTALL to allow 'dot' to match newlines within the dictionary itself.\n        # ([\\s\\S]*?) for non-greedy match of the dictionary content.\n        strategy_line_pattern = r\"{agent_id_escaped} \\(Gen \\d+\\): Total Reward = [\\d.]+[\\s\\S]*?action_strategy = defaultdict\\(<function <lambda> at 0x[0-9a-fA-F]+>, (\\s*{{[\\s\\S]*?}})\\s*\\)\".format(agent_id_escaped=agent_id_escaped)\n\n        matches = list(re.finditer(strategy_line_pattern, log_content, re.DOTALL))\n        \n        if not matches:\n            # print(f\"Warning: No strategy lines found for {agent_id}.\")\n            continue\n            \n        last_match = matches[-1] # Get the last match,\
    \ which should be the final strategy\n        strategy_str = last_match.group(1) # The captured group is the dict part\n        \n        # Sanitize the string to be valid JSON\n        strategy_str = strategy_str.replace(\"'\", \"\\\"\")\n        strategy_str = re.sub(r\",(\\s*})\", r\"\\1\", strategy_str) # Remove trailing comma\n        \n        try:\n            strategy_dict = json.loads(strategy_str)\n            final_strategies[agent_id] = strategy_dict\n        except json.JSONDecodeError as e:\n            print(f\"Warning: Could not decode JSON strategy for {agent_id}: {e}\")\n            print(f\"  String: {strategy_str[:200]}...\")\n            \n    return final_strategies\n\ndef extract_general_info(log_content: str) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Extracts general simulation info like generation, num_agents, num_rounds.\"\"\"\n    info = {}\n    \n    gen_match = re.search(r\"Generation (\\d+), Agents: (\\d+),\", log_content)\n    if gen_match:\n        info['generation_id']\
    \ = int(gen_match.group(1))\n        info['num_agents'] = int(gen_match.group(2))\n    \n    rounds_match = re.search(r\"Starting (\\d+) Rounds of\", log_content)\n    if rounds_match:\n        info['num_rounds'] = int(rounds_match.group(1))\n        \n    return info\n\n# Example Usage (won't run in sandbox directly, but for local testing)\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    mock_jsonl_content = \"\"\"\n    {\"eval_id\": 437, \"log_content\": \"PYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\\\\nSTDOUT:\\\\n...\\\\n  Agent_1 (Gen 1): Total Reward = 1000.0\\\\n    action_strategy = defaultdict(<function <lambda> at 0x...>, {'gather_wood': {'value_est': 0.8}, 'craft_foundation': {'value_est': 0.6}})\\\\n--- Simulation Complete (Generation 1)\\\"}\"\n    {\"eval_id\": 443, \"log_content\": \"PYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\\\\nSTDOUT:\\\\n...\\\\n  Agent_1 (Gen 2): Total Reward = 1200.0\\\\n    action_strategy = defaultdict(<function <lambda> at 0x...>, {'gather_wood': {'value_est': 0.85}, 'craft_foundation': {'value_est':\
    \ 0.7}})\\\\n--- Simulation Complete (Generation 2)\\\"}\"\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    # Mock load_jsonl_log_blocks\n    mock_log_blocks = load_jsonl_log_blocks(\"non_existent_file.jsonl\") # Should report error\n    \n    # Simulate a manually parsed block for strategy extraction\n    sample_log_content_for_strategy = \"\"\"\n    PYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\n    STDOUT:\n    Executing command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\n    --- Starting 2000 Rounds of Transgenerational Building Task (Generation 1, Agents: 5, Initial Complexity) ---\n      Agent_1 (Gen 1): Total Reward = 1170037.5\n        Specialization: Most=gather_wood, Index=0.32\n        Rep for Agent_2: 1.00\n        action_strategy = defaultdict(<function <lambda> at 0x...>, {'gather_wood': {'success': 1, 'attempts': 2, 'value_est': 0.8}, 'craft_foundation': {'success': 1, 'attempts': 2, 'value_est': 0.6}})\n    --- Simulation Complete (Generation 1) ---\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    mock_agent_ids = [f\"Agent_{i+1}\" for\
    \ i in range(5)]\n    extracted_strategies = extract_final_agent_strategies(sample_log_content_for_strategy, mock_agent_ids)\n    \n    print(\"\\nExtracted Strategies (Mock Log for Strategy):\")\n    for agent_id, strategy in extracted_strategies.items():\n        print(f\"  {agent_id}: {json.dumps(strategy, indent=2)[:200]}...\")\n        \n    general_info = extract_general_info(sample_log_content_for_strategy)\n    print(\"\\nExtracted General Info (Mock Log for Strategy):\")\n    print(general_info)\n\n```\n---\n**shared/agency_lab/utilities/logs_to_jsonl_v0_2.py:**\n```\n# Combine raw eval logs into JSONL under shared path; configurable via env vars.\n# Default IN_DIR: storage/shared/agency_lab/data/progressor/raw_eval_logs\n# Default OUT:    storage/shared/agency_lab/data/progressor/raw_eval_logs/all_transgen_logs.jsonl\nimport os, json, glob\n\nIN_DIR = os.environ.get(\"LOGS_IN_DIR\", os.path.join(\"storage\",\"shared\",\"agency_lab\",\"data\",\"progressor\",\"raw_eval_logs\"\
    ))\nOUT    = os.environ.get(\"LOGS_OUT\", os.path.join(IN_DIR, \"all_transgen_logs.jsonl\"))\n\ndef main():\n    os.makedirs(IN_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n    paths = sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(IN_DIR, \"eval_*.txt\")))\n    count = 0\n    with open(OUT, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fout:\n        for p in paths:\n            name = os.path.basename(p)\n            try:\n                eval_id = int(name.split(\"_\")[1].split(\".\")[0])\n            except Exception:\n                eval_id = -1\n            with open(p, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fin:\n                raw = fin.read()\n            fout.write(json.dumps({\"eval_id\": eval_id, \"raw\": raw}, ensure_ascii=False) + \"\\n\")\n            count += 1\n    print(\"WROTE\", OUT, \"records=\", count)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help\
    \ room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
