  The next step will be to call the `extract_final_agent_strategies` function on this single log, with the correct agent IDs, and print the resulting strategies.  This will validate the entire data loading and extraction process. It''s crucial to confirm that the strategy extraction works on an individual log before scaling up to all generations.  This is a proof-of-concept to make sure there are no errors in my parsing of the raw data.


  Once this is confirmed, I can then write a script to iterate over *all* the `gen_*.json` files and create the data structure required by `strategy_extractor.py`.

