    \ `hist_<lineage>.csv`, `outliers.json`) that can help me understand baseline patterns and deviations, which are precursors to emergent novelty.\n\nMy plan for this turn is to submit a Python script that executes the `diagnostics` command using `cli.py`, utilizing its default parameters.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Run Consensus v2.7 Diagnostics for Phantom Sim Data\"\ntags: \"consensus, phantom framework, diagnostics, data analysis, metrics\"\nabstract: \"This script executes the 'diagnostics' command from shared/consensus_v1_5/cli.py to generate diagnostic outputs (per-run CSV, histograms, outliers) for existing phantom simulation data. This will help in understanding the baseline behavior of consensus metrics and identifying potential areas for novelty detection based on deviations or emergent patterns.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import os\n  \n  # Add the consensus_v1_5 directory to the Python path\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/consensus_v1_5')\n\n\
