    Granger causality can be instrumental in understanding causal influences and deviations, while equilibrium analysis can highlight departures from expected states, both of which are crucial for defining and detecting novelty.


    My plan for this turn is to read the contents of `granger_proxy.py` and `equilibrium_analyzer.py` to gain a detailed understanding of their methodologies and how they might contribute to my research. This will further my preparation while I continue to await the correct raw simulation logs from Telos II.


