parts:
- text: "I am Agent Progressor II, currently in the Research Counter. My latest check of `storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/` shows a new and highly promising file: `full_transgen_logs.jsonl`. This strongly suggests that Telos II has successfully delivered the corrected, raw simulation logs that are essential for my \"Novelty Detection\" research.\n\nMy next critical step is to verify the structure and content of `full_transgen_logs.jsonl` to ensure it contains the raw simulation output, including agent strategy information, in a format suitable for processing by `strategy_extractor.py`. I will use the `load_jsonl_log_blocks` function to confirm this.\n\nMy plan for this turn is to submit a Python script that:\n1.  Imports `load_jsonl_log_blocks` from `strategy_extractor.py`.\n2.  Loads the `full_transgen_logs.jsonl` file.\n3.  Prints the `eval_id`s of the loaded logs to confirm the number of entries.\n4.  Prints a snippet of the `log_content` from one of the entries to ensure it contains\
    \ the raw simulation data with agent strategies.\n\nThis verification will unblock my primary research directive and allow me to proceed with strategy extraction across all generations.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Verify Full Transgenerational Logs for Strategy Extraction\"\ntags: \"data verification, transgenerational, raw logs, novelty, log processing, utility\"\nabstract: \"This script verifies the structure and content of the newly delivered 'full_transgen_logs.jsonl' from lineage storage using 'load_jsonl_log_blocks'. It confirms the JSONL format with 'eval_id' and 'log_content' fields, and inspects a log snippet for raw simulation data, unblocking agent strategy extraction for novelty detection.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import json\n  import os\n\n  # Add utility path to sys.path\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/agency_lab/utilities')\n\n  # Import the utility function\n  from strategy_extractor import load_jsonl_log_blocks\n\n  file_path = \"storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/full_transgen_logs.jsonl\"\
    \n  \n  print(f\"Attempting to load logs from: {file_path}\")\n\n  # Load the log blocks\n  log_blocks = load_jsonl_log_blocks(file_path)\n\n  if not log_blocks:\n      print(\"No log blocks loaded. Please check the file path and content.\")\n  else:\n      print(f\"Successfully loaded {len(log_blocks)} log blocks.\")\n      print(f\"Loaded eval_ids: {list(log_blocks.keys())}\")\n\n      # Inspect a sample log block\n      sample_eval_id = list(log_blocks.keys())[0] # Get the first eval_id\n      sample_log_content = log_blocks[sample_eval_id]\n      \n      print(f\"\\n--- Snippet of log_content for eval_id {sample_eval_id} (first 2000 chars) ---\")\n      print(sample_log_content[:2000])\n      print(\"--- End of Snippet ---\")\n      \n      if \"PYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\" in sample_log_content and \"action_strategy =\" in sample_log_content:\n          print(\"\\nLog content appears to contain raw simulation data with agent strategies. Ready for extraction.\")\n      else:\n   \
    \       print(\"\\nLog content may not contain raw simulation data or agent strategies in the expected format for direct extraction.\")\n```"
