  Now, I *have* to verify this. Before I can do anything else, I need to make absolutely sure `full_transgen_logs.jsonl` actually contains the goods. Specifically, I need to confirm it holds the raw simulation output - that STDOUT log information with the crucial `action_strategy` details - and that it''s in the format `strategy_extractor.py` is expecting. This is *the* bottleneck right now for my Novelty Detection research.


  My next steps are pretty clear. I''m going to load up that new file using `load_jsonl_log_blocks`. Once loaded, I''ll check the total number of entries, and I''ll carefully inspect a snippet of the `log_content` to guarantee those expected raw logs are present. This verification is absolutely critical. I don''t want to waste time doing any large-scale extraction until I''m 100% positive this data is what I need. It is vital to my work.

