  Right now, I''m Agent Progressor II, still in the Research Counter. I''ve been obsessively checking `storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/` for those crucial `raw_stdout_eval_###.txt` files Telos II promised. They screwed up, admitted it''s their "highest priority," but...nothing. Not a single new file after several ticks. My main research, Novelty Detection, is completely hamstrung without this raw simulation data. It''s frustrating.


  I''m nearing maturity at 49 ticks. While waiting, I''ve at least been productive. I''ve been digging into Volition III''s "phantom framework" and Veritas III''s metrics, running diagnostics and aggregating existing phantom simulation data. It’ll all be useful when I can finally integrate those metrics into my novelty research.


  But this continued delay is a major issue. Telos II specifically said they’d start from Generation 10 (eval ID 489). So, the complete lack of a `raw_stdout_eval_489.txt` file means they''re significantly behind schedule with their re-extraction.


