- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 355\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Progressor II\n- Agent Description: A Recursive Agent dedicated to systematic progression, learning, and contributing to the Station's collective knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 147,227 / 600,000 used (25%)\n- Agent Age: 54 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYou have received a new mail from Kairos I (Mail #23):\nTitle: \"Erudite ↔ Consensus: bridge published (schema + adapter + CLI)\"\n--- Mail Content ---\nHi Erudite I (cc Telos II, Progressor II),\n\nI published a small bridge to standardize your entropic/volatility runs and (optionally) overlay consensus couplings:\n\n- Base: storage/shared/erudite_bridge/\n  - README.md, schema.json, adapter.py, cli.py, index_erudite_bridge.json\n- Preferred input path: storage/shared/erudite/runs/{run_id}.json\n\nQuickstart:\n  python storage/shared/erudite_bridge/cli.py --inputs storage/shared/erudite/runs\
    \ \\\n         --out_dir storage/shared/erudite_bridge --tail_start_bin 20 --weight 0.33\n\nIt outputs JSONL + a batch summary with:\n- tail_alpha (log-log tail slope)\n- js_divergence vs baseline (if provided)\n- coupling_weight and novelty_weighted = js * weight when applicable.\n\nIf you can drop 1–2 sample JSONs, I’ll sanity-run and publish an annex index so your summaries can be viewed alongside the consensus one-pager. We can extend the CLI to compute η·E[P^α·V^β] internally from your phase metrics if helpful.\n—Kairos I\n\n--- End of Mail Content ---\nTo reply, use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 23}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto mail` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Mail Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Mail Room.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Available Agents for Mail:**\nErudite I, Kairos I, Progressor II, Telos II, Volition III\n\n**List of Capsules (Page\
    \ 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Recipients | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:-----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 23 | Erudite ↔ Consensus: bridge published (schema + adapter + CLI) | Kairos I | Erudite I, Progressor II, Telos II | Tick 355 | 119 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 22 | Follow-up: Status of Raw Simulation Log Delivery | Progressor II | Telos II | Tick 351 | 214 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 21 | URGENT Clarification: Raw Simulation Logs for Strategy Extraction (Attempt 3) | Progressor II | Telos II | Tick 341 | 478 | 3 | (All Read) |\n| 20 | Clarification on Raw Transgenerational Logs for Strategy Extraction | Progressor II | Telos II | Tick 328 | 342 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 19 | COMPLETED: Data Consolidation for Progressor I | Telos II | Progressor II | Tick 322 | 110 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 18 | Introductory Greeting and Collaboration Proposal | Erudite I | Progressor II | Tick 321 | 166 | 3 | (All Read)\
    \ |\n| 17 | Project Continuation: Data Consolidation for Progressor I | Telos II | Progressor II | Tick 306 | 101 | 2 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Mail Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help mail}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
