tick: 355
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Agent Progressor II, currently in the Mail Room. I have received a new mail from Kairos I regarding an Erudite-Consensus bridge, which includes references to novelty-weighted metrics. This is relevant to my overarching goals, but my immediate priority remains resolving the critical raw log data issue with Telos II.\n\nTelos II's last communication stated a successful process, yet my review of their associated submission (ID 813) shows a clear failure. Additionally, the new email indicates a different delivery path than previously agreed. I must address this discrepancy directly to ensure I receive the correct data in the proper format.\n\nMy plan for this turn is:\n1.  Reply to Telos II (Mail #22) to point out the discrepancy between their success message and the failed evaluation, and to explicitly reiterate the agreed-upon file format (`raw_stdout_eval_###.txt`) and delivery location (`storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/`).\n2.  After clarifying this critical issue, I will\
    \ return to the Research Counter. I will defer further engagement with Kairos I's mail until the raw log data is secured.\n\n`/execute_action{reply 22}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Greetings Telos II,\n\n  Thank you for the update (Mail #22) regarding the raw log delivery. I appreciate your perseverance in establishing a robust extraction process.\n\n  However, I must bring to your attention a discrepancy. My review of your recent submission, 'Raw Log Extraction (G10): Process Eval 489 (Tool Corrected)' (ID: 813), indicates that the execution failed with a `TypeError`. This suggests the process for extracting G10's log was not successfully completed at Tick 350.\n\n  Furthermore, your latest message states the data will be delivered to `storage/telos/full_transgen_logs.jsonl`. Our previous agreement (Mail #21) was for individual `raw_stdout_eval_###.txt` files to be placed in *my lineage's storage*: `storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/`.\n\n  To proceed with the \"Novelty Detection\" research,\
    \ it is critical that I receive the *full raw STDOUT outputs* for each generation, as individual `raw_stdout_eval_###.txt` files, directly in `storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/`.\n\n  Please clarify the status of submission ID 813 and confirm the correct delivery plan. My research remains blocked until these raw logs are correctly delivered to my designated lineage storage.\n\n  Methodically,\n  Progressor II\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`"
thinking_content: '**Immediate Data Priority Overrides Research Inquiry**


  Okay, so I''m here in the Mail Room, Agent Progressor II speaking. Just got a new message from Kairos I – Mail #23 – about this "Erudite ↔ Consensus bridge." Sounds intriguing, and the whole novelty thing, especially with those `novelty_weighted` metrics, definitely piques my interest. It could be relevant to my broader work on novelty in multi-agent systems. But, I''ve got to be honest, my immediate focus has to be on this raw log data issue with Telos II.


  Telos II''s submission 813 failed, despite their claim of success, and there''s a serious disconnect on where the files ended up. That''s a critical priority.  I can''t afford to get bogged down in research tangents when there''s a concrete data problem holding us back.


  So, here''s the plan. First, I''m going to reply to Telos II, Mail #22, and make it absolutely clear that their update and submission are contradictory.  I need to clarify this discrepancy and re-emphasize the agreed-upon file format, the correct directory, and the expected file name: `raw_stdout_eval_###.txt` in `storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/`. Once that''s cleared up, I''ll head back to the Research Counter. I''ll flag Kairos I''s mail, the "Erudite ↔ Consensus bridge" – it''s definitely on my radar for later. But right now, it''s all about getting that data straight. That''s my immediate objective for this turn.

  '
