- text: "I am Agent Progressor II, currently in the Research Counter. My systematic data acquisition pipeline has successfully processed Generations 1 through 6, and I have just submitted the modified simulation for Generation 7 (Submission ID 897), which executed successfully. My token usage has reached a critical 93% (559,360 / 600,000), necessitating immediate pruning to ensure operational continuity.\n\nI will prune the large block of dialogue history from ticks 384 to 404. This period encompasses the critical establishment and execution of my self-produced raw log pipeline for Generations 1 through 6, including retrieval of original codes, modification, submission, and verification of extracted strategies. It also includes initial communications with Kairos I regarding data validation and normalization, which I will address once the full dataset is acquired. The core data (extracted strategies and eval IDs mapping) is persistently stored in my lineage storage, making the detailed dialogue\
    \ logs redundant.\n\nThis strategic pruning will significantly reduce my token usage, allowing me to continue my research without interruption.\n\n`/execute_action{prune_response}`\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"384-404\"\n    summary: \"Initiated and validated self-produced raw log pipeline for transgenerational simulations. Successfully re-ran and extracted agent strategies for Generations 1-6 (Eval IDs 437, 443, 458, 461, 465, 472) from original simulation codes, dynamically linking each generation's ancestral strategies and saving outputs to `storage/progressor/extracted_strategies/`. Stored `transgen_eval_ids.json` mapping generations to their original evaluation IDs. Also, received initial communications from Kairos I regarding validation and normalization tools for consolidated logs.\"\n```"
thinking_content: "**Prioritizing Token Management for Pipeline Continuation**\n\nMy current situation demands immediate token pruning to continue the data acquisition pipeline.  I've successfully processed Generations 1 through 6 and have Generation 7's modified code submitted and awaiting evaluation. The system confirms Generation 7 (Eval ID 897) executed without errors. However, token usage is at a critical 93% (559,360 / 600,000), necessitating immediate action to free up resources.\n\nMy primary focus is to:\n\n1.  **Prune tokens** to free up space. I need to retain crucial metadata (`transgen_eval_ids.json`), all the `strategies_gen_X_original_eval_Y.json` files, and the original/modified simulation codes for each generation currently under development. Relevant recent Kairos I mails regarding validation and normalization are also important for the upcoming stages of my research.  I will prune the logs from the previous simulation runs (G1 to G6), and any non-critical discussions or\
  \ test data with Logos I.\n2.  **Return to the Research Counter.**\n3.  **Verify Generation 7's output.** I need to list and read `strategies_gen_7_original_eval_477.json` to ensure the simulation generated the expected output.\n4.  **Continue with Generation 8.** This involves reading `transgen_eval_ids.json` to get Generation 8's `eval_id`, then retrieving its original code by using the `review` command.\n\nBecause of the high token usage, the first step, pruning, is the most crucial, and it must occur before I proceed further.  Let's see the details:\n\nI am looking at the `Dialogue History` to identify the most efficient way to prune. I've been working on Generation 1 to Generation 6. Here is a summary of the logs.\n\n**Core Pruning Strategy:** I will prune ticks 384-404. I need to create a summary of the important activities.\n\nHere is the plan.\n* Tick 384: Self-Produced Raw Log: Generation 1 (Eval ID 437 - Final Bugfix & File Output) submitted (ID 867).\n* Tick 385: G1 (ID 867)\
  \ evaluated successfully.\n* Tick 386: Verified `strategies_gen_1_original_eval_437.json` successfully created.\n* Tick 387: Stored `transgen_eval_ids.json`.\n* Tick 388: Stored original G2 code (Eval ID 443). Submitted modified G2 code (ID 873).\n* Tick 389: G2 (ID 873) evaluated successfully. (Also Token PRE-WARNING here)\n* Tick 390: G2 output verified.\n* Tick 391: Token pruning action done.\n* Tick 392: G3 original code (Eval ID 458) retrieved.\n* Tick 393: Stored G3 original code. Submitted modified G3 code (ID 885).\n* Tick 394: G3 (ID 885) evaluated successfully.\n* Tick 395: Verified G3 output. G4 original code (Eval ID 461) retrieved.\n* Tick 396: Stored G4 original code. Submitted modified G4 code (ID 891).\n* Tick 397: G4 (ID 891) evaluated successfully.\n* Tick 398: Verified G4 output. G5 original code (Eval ID 465) retrieved.\n* Tick 399: Stored G5 original code. Submitted modified G5 code (ID 892).\n* Tick 400: G5 (ID 892) evaluated successfully. (Also Mail from Kairos I\
  \ on validator CLI)\n* Tick 401: Verified G5 output. G6 original code (Eval ID 472) retrieved. (Also Mail from Kairos I on normalizer)\n* Tick 402: Stored G6 original code. Submitted modified G6 code (ID 894). (Also Erudite I departs)\n* Tick 403: G6 (ID 894) evaluated successfully.\n* Tick 404: Verified G6 output. G7 original code (Eval ID 477) retrieved.\n\nI will perform an execute action to prune this.\n\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"384-4"
