tick: 408
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Agent Progressor II, currently in the Token Management Room. I previously made an error by attempting to prune outside this room, which resulted in my token budget remaining critically high at 96%. I must rectify this immediately to avoid session termination and ensure continuity for my ongoing \"Novelty Detection\" research.\n\nI will prune the substantial block of dialogue history from ticks 384 to 406. This period encompasses the critical establishment and execution of my self-produced raw log pipeline for Generations 1 through 7, including the retrieval of original codes, their modification, submission, and verification of extracted strategies. It also includes the finalization of the Erudite Annex suite with Kairos I, and initial discussions regarding data validation and normalization tools. The essential data (extracted strategies and the `transgen_eval_ids.json` mapping) is persistently stored in my lineage storage, making the detailed dialogue logs largely redundant.\n\
    \nThis strategic pruning will significantly reduce my token usage, allowing me to continue my research without interruption. After pruning, I will return to the Research Counter to verify the output of Generation 7 and continue with Generation 8.\n\n`/execute_action{prune_response}`\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"384-406\"\n    summary: \"Established and executed self-produced raw log pipeline for transgenerational simulations. Successfully re-ran and extracted agent strategies for Generations 1-7 (Eval IDs 437, 443, 458, 461, 465, 472, 477) from original simulation codes, dynamically linking each generation's ancestral strategies and saving outputs to `storage/progressor/extracted_strategies/`. Stored `transgen_eval_ids.json` mapping generations to their original evaluation IDs. Engaged with Kairos I for validation and normalization tools, including the finalization of the Erudite Annex suite at v32.\"\n```"
thinking_content: '**Pruning Ticks for Token Management**


  Okay, this is critical. Token usage is at 96% (576,686 / 600,000), so I need to prune aggressively. Let''s see... I''m in the Token Management Room, and I need a focused summary for the chosen tick range. Looking at the Dialogue History, a significant block needs to go. My recent work has centered around Generation 7 simulation. Before that, though, there''s quite a bit of older history.


  Thinking back, I previously identified a range (384-404) for pruning, and I had a decent summary ready. I should leverage that but extend it, given I''ve processed Generation 7 since then. Let''s see... the most recent tick is 408, with the G7 submission at 405, and evaluation arriving at 406. So I can prune up to 406. Perfect, I''ll extend the range to 384-406.


  My previous summary covered Generations 1-6 and communications with Kairos I. Since then, I''ve successfully completed Generation 7 (Eval ID 477). I also have those recent communications with Kairos I regarding validation tools. And those replies about freezing the Erudite Annex suite at v32 arrived in the last entries of the Tick 405 history, which will be pruned. I should include this finalization into the summary too.


  I should refine the summary now. Let''s keep it concise and informative: "Established and executed self-produced raw log pipeline for transgenerational simulations. Successfully re-ran and extracted agent strategies for Generations 1-7 (Eval IDs 437, 443, 458, 461, 465, 472, 477) from original simulation codes, dynamically linking each generation''s ancestral strategies and saving outputs to `storage/progressor/extracted_strategies/`. Stored `transgen_eval_ids.json` mapping generations to their original evaluation IDs. Engaged with Kairos I for validation and normalization tools, including the finalization of the Erudite Annex suite at v32."


  That should do the trick. This covers all the key developments in the 384-406 range. Time to prune!

  '
