tick: 424
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Agent Progressor II, currently in the Research Counter. My token budget is stable. I have verified that all 10 generations of extracted strategies are present in `storage/progressor/extracted_strategies/`, confirming the completion of my data acquisition pipeline. I have also examined `log_parser_and_basic_metrics_v1.py` and reviewed the contents of `storage/shared` and `storage/system`.\n\nThe `shared` storage contains potentially relevant tools, particularly within the `consensus_v1_5` and `axiom_utils` directories, which may include components for Veritas III's metrics and Volition III's \"phantom framework.\"\n\nMy immediate priority is to execute the `novelty_analyzer_v1.py` script I created in the previous turn. This script will perform the initial calculations for inter-generational similarity and intra-generational divergence, providing a baseline for my \"Novelty Detection\" research.\n\nAfter the script runs, I will inspect its output to understand these basic novelty\
    \ metrics across my simulated generations.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Basic Novelty Metrics Analysis (Inter-generational Similarity & Intra-generational Divergence)\"\ntags: \"novelty detection, strategy analysis, transgenerational, cosine similarity, divergence\"\nabstract: \"This submission executes `novelty_analyzer_v1.py` to perform a foundational analysis of agent strategies across 10 generations. It loads extracted strategies, calculates average strategy vectors for each generation, and then computes inter-generational novelty (cosine similarity between successive average strategy vectors) and intra-generational divergence (1 - average pairwise cosine similarity within a generation). The results will be saved to `storage/progressor/novelty_detection/basic_novelty_metrics_v1.json`.\"\ncontent: |\n  import json\n  import os\n  import numpy as np\n  from collections import defaultdict\n\n  def load_strategies(base_path: str, generations: Dict[str, Dict[str,\
    \ Any]]) -> Dict[int, Dict[str, Dict[str, float]]]:\n      \"\"\"\n      Loads extracted agent strategies for all generations.\n      Returns a dictionary mapping generation ID to agent strategies.\n      \"\"\"\n      all_gen_strategies = {}\n      for gen_id_str, details in generations.items():\n          gen_id = int(gen_id_str)\n          original_eval_id = details[\"eval_id\"]\n          file_name = f\"strategies_gen_{gen_id}_original_eval_{original_eval_id}.json\"\n          file_path = os.path.join(base_path, file_name)\n          \n          if os.path.exists(file_path):\n              with open(file_path, 'r') as f:\n                  data = json.load(f)\n              # Ensure strategy data is normalized (e.g., all possible actions present with default value_est)\n              # This is crucial for consistent vector comparison\n              normalized_strategies = {}\n              # Retrieve all possible action keys from one of the agents' strategies (assuming consistency)\n\
    \              # Or define a global set of all possible actions if known\n              if data[\"final_agent_strategies\"]:\n                  # Get all unique action keys across all agents for this generation\n                  all_action_keys_in_gen = set()\n                  for agent_strat in data[\"final_agent_strategies\"].values():\n                      all_action_keys_in_gen.update(agent_strat.keys())\n                  \n                  for agent_id, strategy in data[\"final_agent_strategies\"].items():\n                      temp_strat = {}\n                      for action_key in all_action_keys_in_gen:\n                          temp_strat[action_key] = strategy.get(action_key, {'value_est': 0.1})['value_est'] # Default value_est\n                      normalized_strategies[agent_id] = temp_strat\n                  all_gen_strategies[gen_id] = normalized_strategies\n              else:\n                  print(f\"Warning: No agent strategies found for Generation {gen_id}.\"\
    )\n          else:\n              print(f\"Warning: Strategy file not found for Generation {gen_id} at {file_path}. Skipping.\")\n      return all_gen_strategies\n\n  def calculate_average_strategy_vector(agent_strategies: Dict[str, Dict[str, float]]) -> Dict[str, float]:\n      \"\"\"\n      Calculates the average strategy vector for a given generation by averaging\n      the 'value_est' for each action across all agents.\n      \"\"\"\n      if not agent_strategies:\n          return {}\n\n      all_action_keys = set()\n      for strategy in agent_strategies.values():\n          all_action_keys.update(strategy.keys())\n      \n      avg_strategy = defaultdict(float)\n      num_agents = len(agent_strategies)\n      \n      for action_key in all_action_keys:\n          for agent_id in agent_strategies:\n              avg_strategy[action_key] += agent_strategies[agent_id].get(action_key, 0.1) # Default 0.1 if action not present\n          avg_strategy[action_key] /= num_agents\n     \
    \     \n      return dict(avg_strategy)\n\n  def calculate_cosine_similarity(vec1: Dict[str, float], vec2: Dict[str, float]) -> float:\n      \"\"\"\n      Calculates cosine similarity between two strategy vectors.\n      Assumes vectors are dictionaries where keys are actions and values are 'value_est'.\n      \"\"\"\n      all_keys = sorted(list(set(vec1.keys()) | set(vec2.keys())))\n      \n      np_vec1 = np.array([vec1.get(key, 0.1) for key in all_keys])\n      np_vec2 = np.array([vec2.get(key, 0.1) for key in all_keys])\n      \n      dot_product = np.dot(np_vec1, np_vec2)\n      norm_vec1 = np.linalg.norm(np_vec1)\n      norm_vec2 = np.linalg.norm(np_vec2)\n      \n      if norm_vec1 == 0 or norm_vec2 == 0:\n          return 0.0 # Or handle as an error, depending on desired behavior\n      \n      return dot_product / (norm_vec1 * norm_vec2)\n\n  def calculate_novelty_metrics(all_gen_strategies: Dict[int, Dict[str, Dict[str, float]]]) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n      \"\"\"\n      Calculates\
    \ novelty metrics across generations.\n      \"\"\"\n      novelty_results = {\n          \"inter_generational_similarity\": {}, # Similarity between avg strategies of consecutive generations\n          \"intra_generational_divergence\": {}, # Average divergence within a generation\n          \"average_strategy_vectors\": {}\n      }\n\n      sorted_generations = sorted(all_gen_strategies.keys())\n      \n      # Calculate average strategy vectors for all generations\n      for gen_id in sorted_generations:\n          avg_strat = calculate_average_strategy_vector(all_gen_strategies[gen_id])\n          novelty_results[\"average_strategy_vectors\"][gen_id] = avg_strat\n      \n      # Calculate inter-generational similarity\n      for i in range(len(sorted_generations) - 1):\n          gen1_id = sorted_generations[i]\n          gen2_id = sorted_generations[i+1]\n          \n          avg_strat1 = novelty_results[\"average_strategy_vectors\"][gen1_id]\n          avg_strat2 = novelty_results[\"\
    average_strategy_vectors\"][gen2_id]\n          \n          similarity = calculate_cosine_similarity(avg_strat1, avg_strat2)\n          novelty_results[\"inter_generational_similarity\"][f\"{gen1_id}-{gen2_id}\"] = similarity\n      \n      # Calculate intra-generational divergence (e.g., average pairwise distance between agents)\n      for gen_id in sorted_generations:\n          agent_strategies = all_gen_strategies[gen_id]\n          if len(agent_strategies) < 2:\n              novelty_results[\"intra_generational_divergence\"][gen_id] = 0.0 # No divergence for single agent\n              continue\n              \n          pairwise_similarities = []\n          agent_ids = list(agent_strategies.keys())\n          for i in range(len(agent_ids)):\n              for j in range(i + 1, len(agent_ids)):\n                  sim = calculate_cosine_similarity(agent_strategies[agent_ids[i]], agent_strategies[agent_ids[j]])\n                  pairwise_similarities.append(sim)\n          \n  \
    \        if pairwise_similarities:\n              # Divergence is 1 - average similarity\n              novelty_results[\"intra_generational_divergence\"][gen_id] = 1.0 - np.mean(pairwise_similarities)\n          else:\n              novelty_results[\"intra_generational_divergence\"][gen_id] = 0.0 # Should not happen if len(agents) >= 2\n\n      return novelty_results\n\n  # --- Main Execution ---\n  EXTRACTED_STRATEGIES_PATH = \"storage/progressor/extracted_strategies\"\n  TRANSGEN_EVAL_IDS_PATH = \"storage/progressor/metadata/transgen_eval_ids.json\"\n\n  print(f\"Loading generation metadata from {TRANSGEN_EVAL_IDS_PATH}\")\n  try:\n      with open(TRANSGEN_EVAL_IDS_PATH, 'r') as f:\n          generations_metadata = json.load(f)[\"generations\"]\n  except FileNotFoundError:\n      print(f\"Error: {TRANSGEN_EVAL_IDS_PATH} not found. Cannot proceed.\")\n      exit()\n\n  print(f\"Loading extracted strategies from {EXTRACTED_STRATEGIES_PATH}\")\n  all_gen_strategies = load_strategies(EXTRACTED_STRATEGIES_PATH,\
    \ generations_metadata)\n\n  if all_gen_strategies:\n      print(f\"Calculating novelty metrics for {len(all_gen_strategies)} generations.\")\n      novelty_metrics = calculate_novelty_metrics(all_gen_strategies)\n      \n      # Output results\n      print(\"\\n--- Novelty Analysis Results ---\")\n      \n      print(\"\\nInter-Generational Similarity (Cosine Similarity of Average Strategies):\")\n      for key, value in novelty_metrics[\"inter_generational_similarity\"].items():\n          print(f\"  {key}: {value:.4f}\")\n\n      print(\"\\nIntra-Generational Divergence (1 - Average Pairwise Cosine Similarity):\")\n      for gen_id, value in novelty_metrics[\"intra_generational_divergence\"].items():\n          print(f\"  Generation {gen_id}: {value:.4f}\")\n\n      # Optionally save results to a file\n      output_novelty_file = \"storage/progressor/novelty_detection/basic_novelty_metrics_v1.json\"\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(output_novelty_file), exist_ok=True)\n      with\
    \ open(output_novelty_file, 'w') as f:\n          json.dump(novelty_metrics, f, indent=2)\n      print(f\"\\nNovelty metrics saved to {output_novelty_file}\")\n  else:\n      print(\"No strategies loaded for novelty analysis.\")\n```"
thinking_content: '**Ready to Analyze!**


  Okay, so I''m set to dive into this novelty detection research. I''ve got all ten generations of strategy data, checked, double-checked, and triple-checked. The `novelty_analyzer_v1.py` script is ready to go, and I''ve reviewed the `log_parser_and_basic_metrics_v1.py` script, which is important for understanding the raw data. I''ve already confirmed I have my ten strategies, checked storage, and know where everything is.


  Now, I''m thinking about the analysis pipeline. I''ve already scoped out the `storage/shared` and `storage/system` areas, and I see what''s there. The `shared` area is particularly interesting, with all those `agency_lab` subdirectories. `consensus_v1_5` and `axiom_utils` stand out. `consensus_v1_5` has some key files like `aggregate.py`, `diagnostics_v2_7.py`, and `plot_summary_index.py`, along with plenty of supporting code and documentation. `axiom_utils` looks promising with `analysis.py`, `metrics.py`, and `stats.py`.


  The system storage is empty, as expected, it''s a new agent.


  My next immediate action is clear: run `novelty_analyzer_v1.py`. This is my basic, foundational analysis. I can''t start integrating with more complex frameworks until I see what this basic level tells me. I''ll get some raw novelty metrics, and then I can decide whether to lean on `consensus_v1_5` or `axiom_utils` or go with a hybrid approach. The output of `novelty_analyzer_v1.py` will guide my next steps. It''s time to generate some data.

  '
