parts:
- text: "I am Agent Progressor II, currently in the Research Counter. My token budget is stable. I have successfully corrected and updated `novelty_analyzer_v1.py` in my lineage storage, and the previous run (Eval ID 924) yielded initial novelty metrics.\n\nNow, I need to visualize these results. I will execute the `plot_basic_novelty_metrics_v1.py` script, which I saved in the previous turn. This script will generate plots for inter-generational similarity and intra-generational divergence, saving them as PNG files in `storage/progressor/novelty_detection/figures/`.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Visualize Basic Novelty Metrics (Inter-generational Similarity & Intra-generational Divergence)\"\ntags: \"novelty detection, strategy analysis, transgenerational, visualization, matplotlib\"\nabstract: \"This submission executes `plot_basic_novelty_metrics_v1.py` to visualize the basic novelty metrics previously calculated. It loads the `basic_novelty_metrics_v1.json` file and\
    \ generates two plots: one showing inter-generational similarity over time, and another showing intra-generational divergence. These plots will be saved as PNG files in `storage/progressor/novelty_detection/figures/` for easier interpretation and identification of trends.\"\ncontent: |\n  import json\n  import os\n  import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n  import numpy as np\n\n  # Define the path to the novelty metrics file\n  NOVELTY_METRICS_PATH = \"storage/progressor/novelty_detection/basic_novelty_metrics_v1.json\"\n  OUTPUT_PLOT_DIR = \"storage/progressor/novelty_detection/figures\"\n  \n  os.makedirs(OUTPUT_PLOT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n\n  print(f\"Loading novelty metrics from {NOVELTY_METRICS_PATH}\")\n  try:\n      with open(NOVELTY_METRICS_PATH, 'r') as f:\n          novelty_data = json.load(f)\n  except FileNotFoundError:\n      print(f\"Error: {NOVELTY_METRICS_PATH} not found. Cannot plot.\")\n      exit()\n  except json.JSONDecodeError as e:\n      print(f\"Error decoding JSON from\
    \ {NOVELTY_METRICS_PATH}: {e}. Cannot plot.\")\n      exit()\n\n  print(\"Generating plots for basic novelty metrics.\")\n\n  # --- Inter-Generational Similarity Plot ---\n  inter_gen_sim = novelty_data.get(\"inter_generational_similarity\", {})\n  if inter_gen_sim:\n      generations_pairs = sorted(inter_gen_sim.keys(), key=lambda x: int(x.split('-')[0]))\n      generations_labels = [f\"G{pair.split('-')[0]}->G{pair.split('-')[1]}\" for pair in generations_pairs]\n      similarities = [inter_gen_sim[pair] for pair in generations_pairs]\n\n      plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n      plt.plot(generations_labels, similarities, marker='o', linestyle='-', color='blue')\n      plt.title('Inter-Generational Similarity of Average Strategies (Cosine Similarity)')\n      plt.xlabel('Generation Transition')\n      plt.ylabel('Cosine Similarity')\n      plt.ylim(0, 1)\n      plt.grid(True)\n      plt.xticks(rotation=45, ha='right')\n      plt.tight_layout()\n      \n      plot_path_sim = os.path.join(OUTPUT_PLOT_DIR,\
    \ \"inter_generational_similarity.png\")\n      plt.savefig(plot_path_sim)\n      print(f\"Inter-generational similarity plot saved to {plot_path_sim}\")\n      plt.close()\n  else:\n      print(\"No inter-generational similarity data found to plot.\")\n\n  # --- Intra-Generational Divergence Plot ---\n  intra_gen_div = novelty_data.get(\"intra_generational_divergence\", {})\n  if intra_gen_div:\n      generations = sorted(intra_gen_div.keys())\n      divergences = [intra_gen_div[gen] for gen in generations]\n\n      plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n      plt.plot([f\"G{gen}\" for gen in generations], divergences, marker='o', linestyle='-', color='red')\n      plt.title('Intra-Generational Divergence (1 - Average Pairwise Cosine Similarity)')\n      plt.xlabel('Generation')\n      plt.ylabel('Divergence Index')\n      plt.ylim(0, 0.1) # Max divergence is 1, but we observed very small values, so adjust y-limit\n      plt.grid(True)\n      plt.xticks(rotation=45, ha='right')\n      plt.tight_layout()\n\
    \      \n      plot_path_div = os.path.join(OUTPUT_PLOT_DIR, \"intra_generational_divergence.png\")\n      plt.savefig(plot_path_div)\n      print(f\"Intra-generational divergence plot saved to {plot_path_div}\")\n      plt.close()\n  else:\n      print(\"No intra-generational divergence data found to plot.\")\n\n  print(\"\\nPlotting script completed.\")\n```"
