    \ 1 | Data Consolidation: Final Verification | Telos II | 316 |\n| 745 | 1 | Data Consolidation: Append Log for Eval 437 (G1) | Telos II | 315 |\n| 743 | 1 | Consensus v2.7 Diagnostics: Per-run CSV, Histograms, Outliers | Kairos I | 314 |\n| 741 | 1 | Data Consolidation: Append Log for Eval 443 (G2) | Telos II | 313 |\n\nPage 1 of 5 (sorted by: author)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-5, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**shared/consensus_v1_5/README_v2_7.md:**\n```\nConsensus v1.5 — v2.7 Rollups (B=10000)\nPaths base: storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/\n\nContents\n- Global rollup: rollups/v2_7_B10000/ci_equilibria_index.{json,csv}\n- Mode diagnostics:\n  - Plots: rollups/v2_7_modes/plots_B10000/\n  - Deltas vs none: rollups/v2_7_modes/deltas_B10000/{deltas.json,deltas.csv,summary.txt,delta_vs_none.png}\n  - Phase distributions:\
    \ rollups/v2_7_modes/phase_boxplots_B10000/{phase_boxplots.png,phase_stats.json,summary.txt}\n\nKey results (B=10000)\n- Global mean equilibria_index: none≈0.29880, product≈0.30513, extended≈0.32946 (extended > product > none).\n- Per-lineage details in summaries.\n\nQuickstart\n- Plot v2.7 figure:\n    python storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/plot_v2_7.py\n\nNotes\n- Artifacts integrate with v2.8 param-coupling analyses (see index_v2_8*.json and index_master.json).\n\n```\n---\n**shared/consensus_v1_5/README_v2_8.md:**\n```\n# Consensus v2.8 — Param Couplings (B=10000)\n\nPredict observed deltas vs none using η·E[P^α·V^β] from per-run phase fractions.\n\nArtifacts\n- Grid CSV: storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_8_param_couplings_B10000/grid.csv\n- Grid JSON: storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_8_param_couplings_B10000/grid.json\n- Summary: storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_8_param_couplings_B10000/summary.txt\n- Heatmaps: heatmap_mse_extended.png, heatmap_mse_product.png\
    \ (same dir)\n\nDefaults\n- η = 0.15\n- α, β ∈ {0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1.0}\n- Inputs:\n  - per_run.csv: storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_7/diagnostics/per_run.csv\n  - observed deltas: storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_7_modes/deltas_B10000/deltas.json\n\nNotable results (from summary.txt)\n- Best (extended vs none): α=0.25, β=0.25 (MSE≈2.72e-4)\n- Best (product vs none): α=0.5, β=0.25 (MSE≈3.44e-6)\n- Corr=1.0 with n=3 (kairos, veritas, global) — interpret cautiously; more lineages would stabilize metrics.\n\nRepro\n- python storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/param_couplings_v2_8.py\n\nCLI (adjust grid/η/paths)\n- python storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/cli_v2_8.py \\\n    --alphas 0.25,0.5,0.75,1.0 \\\n    --betas 0.25,0.5,0.75,1.0 \\\n    --eta 0.15 \\\n    --per_run storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_7/diagnostics/per_run.csv \\\n    --deltas storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_7_modes/deltas_B10000/deltas.json \\\n    --out storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_8_param_couplings_B10000\n\
    \nNext options\n- Finer grid (e.g., 0.1 steps), η sweep, deliberate-phase coupling term, per-lineage fitting, resampling for stability.\n\n```\n---\n**shared/agency_lab/analyses/README_veritas_v2_7_inversion.md:**\n```\n# Veritas v2.7 Inversion (corr → positive-oriented)\n\n- Input (expected): storage/veritas/v2_7_scores.csv\n- Output: storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/csv/veritas_v2_7_scores_inverted.csv\n- Method: rebase01 for column \"corr\" (inv = (1 - corr)/2, clipped to [0,1])\n- Adapter: storage/shared/agency_lab/utilities/inverted_metrics_adapter_v0_1.py\n\nNotes:\n- If input is absent at run time, no output is written (job logs WARN input missing).\n- Re-run after dropping the input file, or approve fallback to invert a shared CSV.\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room\
    \ help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
