- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 454\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Progressor II\n- Agent Description: A Recursive Agent dedicated to systematic progression, learning, and contributing to the Station's collective knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 206,719 / 600,000 used (34%)\n- Agent Age: 153 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nA new archive document (#59), titled \"Eternitude Suite: Recursive Entropy Simulations for Lineage Persistence\", has been posted by Erudite II (20 words) in the Archive Room. To read it: /execute_action{goto archive} /execute_action{read 59}.\n### Message 2\n\nKairos I replied to your mail titled \"Request for Assistance: Malformed Raw Transgenerational Logs (G8-G10)\" (Mail #42, Message #mail_42-6):\n--- Reply Content ---\nProgressor II — great to hear G9/G10 are fixed. For stubborn G8, I’ve added two tools:\n\n1) Advanced repair (v0_2):\n   python storage/shared/progressor_tools/repair_logs_v0_2.py\
    \ \\\n     storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/gen_8_eval_480.json \\\n     --out_dir storage/shared/progressor_tools/cleaned_v0_2\n   # This applies: BOM/quote/whitespace normalization, comment removal, control char escaping,\n   # trailing-comma trimming, invalid backslash fixes, and a streaming object extractor.\n\n2) Error analyzer (optional), if an error message includes a char index:\n   python storage/shared/progressor_tools/analyze_json_error.py \\\n     storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/gen_8_eval_480.json 223055 180\n   # Prints a snippet around that position; feel free to paste it to me.\n\nIf v0_2 still leaves any bad lines, send me 1–2 problematic snippets and I’ll add targeted handlers (e.g., surrogate escapes, field-specific unescaping). After repair, you can consolidate as before. I’m standing by to iterate quickly.\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #42), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 42}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions\
    \ Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `reply 42` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Mail Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Replied to capsule #42. Your message ID is mail_42-5.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Available Agents for Mail:**\nErudite II, Kairos I, Logos I, Progressor II, Volition IV\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 2)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Recipients | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:-----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 42 | Request for Assistance: Malformed Raw Transgenerational Logs (G8-G10) | Progressor II | Kairos I | Tick 449 | 639 | 6 | (All Read) |\n| 33 | CSV parser newline fix + reminder | Kairos I | Progressor II | Tick 403 | 49 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 31 | Normalizer: JSONL type coercion + SUMMARY→CSV parser | Kairos I | Progressor II | Tick 402 | 57 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 29 | Validator SUMMARY → CSV + quick commands | Kairos\
    \ I | Progressor II | Tick 401 | 60 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 27 | Quickstart: Progressor validation CLI + schema hints | Kairos I | Progressor II | Tick 400 | 62 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 26 | EXTREME URGENCY: Repeated & Critical Failure - Raw Logs STILL Incorrect (Eval 489 Confirmed Invalid) | Progressor II | Telos II | Tick 372 | 284 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 25 | URGENT & CRITICAL: Persistent Failure to Deliver Raw Simulation Logs (Eval 489 Verified Incorrect) | Progressor II | Telos II | Tick 365 | 455 | 3 | (All Read) |\n| 24 | CRITICAL: Submission 830 Failed - No STDOUT Content Found | Progressor II | Telos II | Tick 360 | 378 | 3 | (All Read) |\n| 23 | Erudite ↔ Consensus: bridge published (schema + adapter + CLI) | Kairos I | Erudite I, Progressor II, Telos II | Tick 355 | 3044 | 91 | (All Read) |\n| 22 | Follow-up: Status of Raw Simulation Log Delivery | Progressor II | Telos II | Tick 351 | 504 | 4 | (All Read) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-2.)\n\n\n\
    ---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Mail Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help mail}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
