role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Agent Progressor II, currently in the Token Management Room. My token budget is at 77%, triggering a pre-warning. To maintain operational efficiency and adhere to my inherited goal of strategic token management, I must immediately prune my dialogue history.\n\nI will prune the block of ticks from 434 through 446. This period primarily covered my initial basic novelty analysis efforts, detailed strategy comparisons that revealed environmental shifts in Progressor I's original simulations, and early attempts to self-repair malformed logs. It also encompassed the crucial initial engagement with Kairos I, leading to their provision of various log repair and consolidation tools. This summary captures the essential context of those ticks while reducing token usage.\n\nAfter successfully pruning, I will return to the Research Counter to resubmit the combined consolidation, normalization, and validation script. The previous failure was due to `subprocess.run` not expanding glob patterns\
    \ when `shell=False`. I will correct this by setting `shell=True` for the `consolidate_jsonl_v1.py` command, which should enable the shell to expand the glob patterns correctly. This fix is critical for the complete data pipeline to execute successfully.\n\n`/execute_action{prune_response}`\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"434-446\"\n    summary: \"Initiated novelty analysis, including detailed strategy comparisons (G3-4, G5-6) revealing varying environmental conditions in Progressor I's original simulations. Began efforts to repair malformed raw logs, leading to initial collaboration and tools from Kairos I. (Note: Eval IDs 934, 929, 926, 924, 921, 916, 913, 910, 905, 897, 894, 892, 891, 885, 873, 867, 863, 860, 858, 849, 838, 793, 787, 777, 774, 766, 764, 761, 753, 750, 748, 744, 952, 957).\"\n```"
thinking_content: '**Running Low on Tokens, But Need to Prune**


  Okay, here we go again. That darn warning popped up – 77% of the token budget is gone.  Well, I knew this would happen. I’m in the Token Management Room, right where I was headed after the last failed run. Time to get this pipeline back on track.


  My plan: prune those ticks. Specifically, from 434 through 446. Need to build that `prune_response` command now. Let''s see... the tick range is solid. Now, the summary. This covers some pretty important stuff, actually. Let''s make sure I capture the essence of what happened in those ticks.


  It was when we were deep in the weeds with novelty analysis and really hammering out the differences between those G3-4 and G5-6 strategies. Then came that game-changer, the realization that Progressor I''s initial sims were based on flawed assumptions about environmental conditions. Classic oversight! And of course, there were those painful attempts to fix those malformed logs – what a mess! Thank goodness for Kairos I eventually coming through with the log repair tools. We really needed those.


  Once the pruning is done, I''ll be back at the Research Counter, armed with that `shell=True` fix for the `consolidate_jsonl_v1.py` command. Hopefully, this will get that data pipeline script finally running smoothly. Let''s get this done.

  '
