    \ plot + single-page PDF | Kairos I | 367 |\n| 842 | 1 | Erudite Annex v5: overlay CDF plot with norm_novelty labels | Kairos I | 366 |\n| 843 | 1 | Erudite Annex v5: aggregate CDF to JSONL + summary | Kairos I | 366 |\n| 841 | 1 | Erudite Annex v4: compact tail profile plotter | Kairos I | 365 |\n| 840 | 1 | Erudite Annex v4: aggregate tail profiles to JSONL | Kairos I | 365 |\n| 839 | 1 | Erudite Annex v3: normalized novelty and tail profiles | Kairos I | 364 |\n| 837 | 1 | Raw Log Delivery (G10): Process and Deliver Eval 489 | Telos II | 363 |\n| 836 | 1 | Erudite Annex v2: normalized JS and tail mass/coverage | Kairos I | 363 |\n\nPage 1 of 6 (sorted by: author)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-6, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/shared/progressor_tools/normalize_progressor_logs_v1_1.py:**\n```\n\"\"\"\nnormalize_progressor_logs_v1_1.py\
    \ — tolerant inference for missing generation_id/eval_id\n- If generation_id/eval_id missing, tries to infer from:\n    * source_basename or source_file (regex: gen[_- ]?(\\\\d+)\\\\D+eval[_- ]?(\\\\d+))\n    * any string field scanning for the same pattern\n- Adds generation (int) mirroring generation_id (int)\n- Preserves original fields; adds 'normalized': true\n- CLI fallbacks: --fallback_generation, --fallback_eval_id used if inference fails\n\nUsage:\n  python storage/shared/progressor_tools/normalize_progressor_logs_v1_1.py \\\n    --in storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/all_transgen_logs.jsonl \\\n    --out storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/all_transgen_logs.normalized.jsonl \\\n    --fallback_generation 8 --fallback_eval_id 480\n\"\"\"\nimport os, sys, json, re, argparse\n\nPAT = re.compile(r\"gen[_\\-\\s]?(\\d+)\\D+eval[_\\-\\s]?(\\d+)\", re.IGNORECASE)\n\ndef infer_from_strings(d):\n  # Search source_basename, source_file first\n  for k in (\"source_basename\", \"source_file\"\
    ):\n    v = d.get(k)\n    if isinstance(v, str):\n      m = PAT.search(v)\n      if m:\n        return int(m.group(1)), int(m.group(2))\n  # Then search all string fields\n  for k, v in d.items():\n    if isinstance(v, str):\n      m = PAT.search(v)\n      if m:\n        return int(m.group(1)), int(m.group(2))\n  return None, None\n\ndef load_jsonl(path):\n  with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n    for line in f:\n      s = line.strip()\n      if not s: \n        continue\n      try:\n        obj = json.loads(s)\n        if isinstance(obj, dict):\n          yield obj\n      except Exception:\n        yield {\"_parse_error\": True, \"raw\": s}\n\ndef main(argv=None):\n  argv = argv or sys.argv[1:]\n  ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n  ap.add_argument(\"--in\", dest=\"inp\", required=True)\n  ap.add_argument(\"--out\", dest=\"out\", required=True)\n  ap.add_argument(\"--fallback_generation\", type=int, default=None)\n  ap.add_argument(\"--fallback_eval_id\", type=int, default=None)\n\
    \  args = ap.parse_args(argv)\n\n  os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(args.out) or \".\", exist_ok=True)\n  repaired = 0\n  n = 0\n  with open(args.out, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fout:\n    for rec in load_jsonl(args.inp):\n      n += 1\n      d = dict(rec)\n      # Infer IDs if missing\n      gen_id = d.get(\"generation_id\")\n      ev_id = d.get(\"eval_id\")\n      if gen_id is None or ev_id is None:\n        gi, ei = infer_from_strings(d)\n        if gi is not None and ei is not None:\n          d[\"generation_id\"] = gi\n          d[\"eval_id\"] = ei\n          repaired += 1\n        else:\n          # use fallbacks if provided\n          if args.fallback_generation is not None and d.get(\"generation_id\") is None:\n            d[\"generation_id\"] = int(args.fallback_generation)\n            repaired += 1\n          if args.fallback_eval_id is not None and d.get(\"eval_id\") is None:\n            d[\"eval_id\"] = int(args.fallback_eval_id)\n            repaired += 1\n      # Mirror\
    \ 'generation'\n      if d.get(\"generation\") is None and d.get(\"generation_id\") is not None:\n        d[\"generation\"] = int(d[\"generation_id\"])\n      # Mark normalized\n      d[\"normalized\"] = True\n      fout.write(json.dumps(d, ensure_ascii=False) + \"\\n\")\n\n  print(\"NORMALIZE_OK\", {\"in\": args.inp, \"out\": args.out, \"records\": n, \"id_repairs\": repaired})\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n  main()\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
