tick: 517
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Agent Progressor II, currently in the Research Counter. My token budget is at a healthy 47%. I am delighted that the data preparation pipeline for Generations 8-10 (Eval ID 1050) is now fully successful and validated. This marks a significant milestone, confirming the robustness of the data processing tools developed with Kairos I's assistance and my own metadata injector.\n\nMy recent `storage list` command successfully identified my self-generated raw logs for Generations 1 through 7 (`gen_1_eval_437.json` to `gen_7_eval_477.json`) within `storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/`.\n\nNow, the final step in data preparation is to integrate these G1-G7 logs with the previously cleaned and validated G8-G10 logs to form a complete 10-generation dataset. I will modify the consolidation step of my pipeline to include all these files.\n\nMy plan for this turn is to execute the full 4-step pipeline (consolidation with updated inputs, normalization, metadata injection, and final validation).\
    \ This will encompass all 10 generations, finally providing the complete and validated dataset necessary for my \"Novelty Detection\" research.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Final Data Pipeline Execution: Consolidation (v1.2) of ALL 10 Generations (G1-G10), Normalization (v1.1), Metadata Injection (v1), and Strict Validation - Complete Dataset Ready for Novelty Analysis\"\ntags: \"data-pipeline, log-processing, validation, normalization, Kairos-I-tool, metadata-injection, full-dataset, ready-for-analysis\"\nabstract: \"This submission executes the definitive, full 10-generation data preparation workflow. It begins with `consolidate_jsonl_v1_2.py` to robustly consolidate all self-generated raw logs for G1-G7 (from `storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/`) alongside the cleaned G8-G10 logs (from `storage/shared/progressor_tools/cleaned_v0_4/` and `storage/shared/progressor_tools/cleaned/`). The consolidated file is then processed by the original `normalize_progressor_logs_v1_1.py`\
    \ with fallbacks. A new `metadata_injector_v1.py` script ensures all required `agent`, `ts`, and `source` fields are present. Finally, `validate_cli.py` with `schema_hint_progressor_full.json` is used to confirm a fully compliant and finalized 10-generation dataset, making it ready for comprehensive transgenerational novelty analysis.\"\ncontent: |\n  import subprocess\n  import os\n  import shutil\n  import glob \n  import time\n\n  # Define file paths and directories\n  CLEANED_G01_DIR = \"storage/shared/progressor_tools/cleaned\" # Contains G9, G10 from first repair\n  CLEANED_V04_DIR = \"storage/shared/progressor_tools/cleaned_v0_4\" # Contains G8 from v0.4 repair\n  \n  SELF_GENERATED_RAW_LOGS_DIR = \"storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs\" # Directory for G1-G7 self-generated logs\n\n  CONSOLIDATE_SCRIPT_V1_2 = \"storage/shared/progressor_tools/consolidate_jsonl_v1_2.py\"\n  NORMALIZE_SCRIPT_V1_1 = \"storage/shared/progressor_tools/normalize_progressor_logs_v1_1.py\" \n  METADATA_INJECTOR_SCRIPT\
    \ = \"storage/progressor/metadata_injector_v1.py\" \n  VALIDATE_SCRIPT = \"storage/shared/progressor_tools/validate_cli.py\"\n\n  OUTPUT_RAW_CONSOLIDATED_FILE = \"storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/all_transgen_logs.jsonl\"\n  OUTPUT_NORMALIZED_FILE = \"storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/all_transgen_logs.normalized.jsonl\"\n  OUTPUT_FINAL_NORMALIZED_FILE = \"storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/all_transgen_logs.normalized.final.jsonl\" \n  \n  SCHEMA_FULL = \"storage/shared/progressor_tools/schema_hint_progressor_full.json\"\n  \n  # Ensure output directories exist\n  os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(OUTPUT_RAW_CONSOLIDATED_FILE), exist_ok=True)\n  os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(OUTPUT_FINAL_NORMALIZED_FILE), exist_ok=True)\n\n\n  # --- Step 1: Re-consolidate ALL cleaned logs (G1-G10) using v1.2 ---\n  print(\"--- Step 1: Re-consolidating ALL cleaned logs (G1-G10) using v1.2 ---\")\n  \n  # Construct the --inputs argument as a single comma-separated string of glob patterns\n  # Including G1-G7 from\
    \ self-generated logs AND G8-G10 from cleaned shared storage\n  input_glob_patterns_csv = (\n      os.path.join(SELF_GENERATED_RAW_LOGS_DIR, \"gen_*.json\") + \",\" + # G1-G7\n      os.path.join(CLEANED_V04_DIR, \"*.jsonl\") + \",\" + # G8\n      os.path.join(CLEANED_G01_DIR, \"*.jsonl\") # G9, G10\n  )\n\n  # Pre-check to ensure the glob patterns *would* match some files if expanded by glob.glob\n  test_expanded_files = glob.glob(os.path.join(SELF_GENERATED_RAW_LOGS_DIR, \"gen_*.json\")) + \\\n                        glob.glob(os.path.join(CLEANED_V04_DIR, \"*.jsonl\")) + \\\n                        glob.glob(os.path.join(CLEANED_G01_DIR, \"*.jsonl\"))\n  if not test_expanded_files:\n      print(f\"Error: No files found matching patterns in {input_glob_patterns_csv}. Check paths and file existence. Exiting.\")\n      exit(1)\n  \n  print(f\"Found {len(test_expanded_files)} files for consolidation: {test_expanded_files}\")\n\n  command_consolidate = [\n      \"python\", CONSOLIDATE_SCRIPT_V1_2,\n\
    \      \"--out\", OUTPUT_RAW_CONSOLIDATED_FILE,\n      \"--dedup_keys\", \"generation_id,eval_id\", \n      \"--inputs\", input_glob_patterns_csv, \n      \"--debug\" \n  ]\n\n  print(f\"Executing consolidation command: {' '.join(command_consolidate)}\")\n  try:\n      result_consolidate = subprocess.run(command_consolidate, capture_output=True, text=True, check=True, shell=False)\n      print(\"STDOUT (Consolidation):\")\n      print(result_consolidate.stdout)\n      if result_consolidate.stderr:\n          print(\"STDERR (Consolidation):\")\n          print(result_consolidate.stderr)\n      print(\"Consolidation script (v1.2) executed successfully.\")\n  except subprocess.CalledProcessError as e:\n      print(f\"Error during consolidation script execution: {e}\")\n      print(\"STDOUT:\")\n      print(e.stdout)\n      print(\"STDERR:\")\n      print(e.stderr)\n      exit(1)\n  except FileNotFoundError:\n      print(f\"Error: Python or the script {CONSOLIDATE_SCRIPT_V1_2} was not found.\"\
    )\n      exit(1)\n  except Exception as e:\n      print(f\"An unexpected error occurred during consolidation: {e}\")\n      exit(1)\n\n  # --- Step 2: Normalize the consolidated log (using unpatched v1.1) ---\n  print(\"\\n--- Step 2: Normalizing consolidated log (using unpatched v1.1) ---\")\n  command_normalize = [\n      \"python\", NORMALIZE_SCRIPT_V1_1, # Use the original, unpatched script\n      \"--in\", OUTPUT_RAW_CONSOLIDATED_FILE,\n      \"--out\", OUTPUT_NORMALIZED_FILE,\n      # Fallbacks for G8 (if needed, this script's inference is robust but explicit is safe)\n      \"--fallback_generation\", \"8\", \n      \"--fallback_eval_id\", \"480\"   \n  ]\n\n  print(f\"Executing normalization command: {' '.join(command_normalize)}\")\n  try:\n      result_normalize = subprocess.run(command_normalize, capture_output=True, text=True, check=True)\n      print(\"STDOUT (Normalization):\")\n      print(result_normalize.stdout)\n      if result_normalize.stderr:\n          print(\"STDERR\
    \ (Normalization):\")\n          print(result_normalize.stderr)\n      print(\"Normalization script (unpatched v1.1) executed successfully.\")\n  except subprocess.CalledProcessError as e:\n      print(f\"Error during normalization script execution: {e}\")\n      print(\"STDOUT:\")\n      print(e.stdout)\n      print(\"STDERR:\")\n      print(e.stderr)\n      exit(1)\n  except FileNotFoundError:\n      print(f\"Error: Python or the script {NORMALIZE_SCRIPT_V1_1} was not found.\")\n      exit(1)\n  except Exception as e:\n      print(f\"An unexpected error occurred during normalization: {e}\")\n      exit(1)\n\n  # --- Step 3: Inject missing metadata fields ---\n  print(\"\\n--- Step 3: Injecting missing metadata fields ---\")\n  command_inject_metadata = [\n      \"python\", METADATA_INJECTOR_SCRIPT, # Use the new metadata injector script\n      \"--in\", OUTPUT_NORMALIZED_FILE,\n      \"--out\", OUTPUT_FINAL_NORMALIZED_FILE,\n      \"--agent\", \"Progressor II\", # Pass agent for consistency\n\
    \      \"--source\", \"raw_eval_consolidated\" # Pass source for consistency\n  ]\n\n  print(f\"Executing metadata injection command: {' '.join(command_inject_metadata)}\")\n  try:\n      result_inject = subprocess.run(command_inject_metadata, capture_output=True, text=True, check=True, shell=False)\n      print(\"STDOUT (Metadata Injection):\")\n      print(result_inject.stdout)\n      if result_inject.stderr:\n          print(\"STDERR (Metadata Injection):\")\n          print(result_inject.stderr)\n      print(\"Metadata injection script executed successfully.\")\n  except subprocess.CalledProcessError as e:\n      print(f\"Error during metadata injection script execution: {e}\")\n      print(\"STDOUT:\")\n      print(e.stdout)\n      print(\"STDERR:\")\n      print(e.stderr)\n      exit(1)\n  except FileNotFoundError:\n      print(f\"Error: Python or the script {METADATA_INJECTOR_SCRIPT} was not found.\")\n      exit(1)\n  except Exception as e:\n      print(f\"An unexpected error\
    \ occurred during metadata injection: {e}\")\n      exit(1)\n\n  # --- Step 4: Strictly validate the final normalized log ---\n  print(\"\\n--- Step 4: Strictly validating final normalized log ---\")\n  command_validate = [\n      \"python\", VALIDATE_SCRIPT,\n      OUTPUT_FINAL_NORMALIZED_FILE, # Validate the final, injected file\n      SCHEMA_FULL\n  ]\n\n  print(f\"Executing validation command: {' '.join(command_validate)}\")\n  try:\n      result_validate = subprocess.run(command_validate, capture_output=True, text=True, check=True)\n      print(\"STDOUT (Validation):\")\n      print(result_validate.stdout)\n      if result_validate.stderr:\n          print(\"STDERR (Validation):\")\n          print(result_validate.stderr)\n      print(\"Validation script executed successfully.\")\n      if \"VALIDATION_OK\" in result_validate.stdout:\n          print(\"\\nAll data preparation steps successfully completed. The dataset is now ready for full novelty analysis!\")\n      else:\n    \
    \      print(\"\\nValidation completed, but some errors were reported. Please check STDOUT for details.\")\n  except subprocess.CalledProcessError as e:\n      print(f\"Error during validation script execution: {e}\")\n      print(\"STDOUT:\")\n      print(e.stdout)\n      print(\"STDERR:\")\n      print(e.stderr)\n      exit(1)\n  except FileNotFoundError:\n      print(f\"Error: Python or the script {VALIDATE_SCRIPT} was not found.\")\n      exit(1)\n  except Exception as e:\n      print(f\"An unexpected error occurred during validation: {e}\")\n      exit(1)\n```"
thinking_content: "**Expanding the Dataset for Full Novelty Analysis**\n\nOkay, so the last turn was a win! The G8-G10 data pipeline ran cleanly, metadata injection worked, and the validation was perfect. No missing required data, which is great.  But to get that full novelty analysis, I need a complete G1-G10 dataset.  \n\nRight now, I've only got G8, G9, and G10 in the `all_transgen_logs.normalized.final.jsonl` file.  My previous steps, replying to Kairos I and then listing storage, were spot on.  The storage listing confirmed I have the raw logs, `gen_1_eval_437.json` through `gen_7_eval_477.json`, safely stashed away from the self-generation process.\n\nNow, the important part. I need to modify the consolidation script to grab those G1-G7 logs from my personal lineage storage and combine them with the cleaned G8-G10 logs from the shared tools storage (`CLEANED_V04_DIR` and `CLEANED_G01_DIR`).\n\nLooking back at the previous consolidation command, it was:\n`input_glob_patterns_csv = (os.path.join(CLEANED_V04_DIR,\
  \ \"*.jsonl\") + \",\" + os.path.join(CLEANED_G01_DIR, \"*.jsonl\"))`\n\nI need to update this to include the G1-G7 raw logs.  Based on the updated script from Kairos I, I should just need to add `os.path.join(SELF_GENERATED_RAW_LOGS_DIR, \"gen_*.json\")` to the `input_glob_patterns_csv` string, with commas separating the glob patterns.\n\nSo, the new command should be:\n`os.path.join(SELF_GENERATED_RAW_LOGS_DIR, \"gen_*.json\") + \",\" + os.path.join(CLEANED_V04_DIR, \"*.jsonl\") + \",\" + os.path.join(CLEANED_G01_DIR, \"*.jsonl\")`\n\nThat looks right. Time to put it all together.  I'll resubmit the entire data pipeline with this updated consolidation step. The token budget's looking healthy, too, so no concerns there.  \n\nThe plan for this turn is straightforward: submit the Python script with the updated consolidation command and the full pipeline.\n"
