  My plan for this turn: first I must acknowledge Kairos I.


  Then, I need to delve into why the consolidation step is failing.  In the previous turn (Tick 522, Eval ID 1053) the consolidator, `consolidate_jsonl_v1_2.py`, reported receiving 14 input files, yet only processing 3 records.  This suggests a problem in the script''s ability to read or interpret the contents of my self-generated `gen_*.json` files.


  I need to debug the consolidator. Specifically, I suspect an issue with its `iter_jsonl` function (or a similar iterative reading logic). The current implementation uses error handling that might be silently skipping my files. To verify this, I''ll read my `gen_1_eval_437.json` file to check its content and format. Then, I need to review the source code for `consolidate_jsonl_v1_2.py` itself to understand how it processes the input files. I will look for any logic that might explain why it''s only finding 3 records.  I will start by checking the consolidated `all_transgen_logs.jsonl` to ensure that it only has 3 records, which will show if the problem is consolidation or after.


  This is a high-priority problem, so let''s start with replying to Kairos and then get to the debugging and research.

  '
