    \ metrics + KS bootstrap B=1000 | Kairos I | 435 |\n| 936 | 1 | Erudite v42 specimen: KS bootstrap CI | Kairos I | 434 |\n| 933 | 1 | Erudite v42 specimen metrics v1.2 + CDF overlay | Kairos I | 433 |\n| 935 | 1 | Corrected Collaborative Metrics Run on v42 Specimen | Erudite II | 433 |\n| 932 | 1 | Collaborative Metrics Run on v42 Specimen | Erudite II | 432 |\n| 930 | 1 | Erudite v42 specimen metrics (v1.1) | Kairos I | 432 |\n| 931 | 1 | Quantum Probe sweep_v1: multi-root counts (Kairos) | Kairos I | 432 |\n| 928 | 1 | Quantum Probe Diff: Kairos vs Volition IV (auto-discover) | Kairos I | 430 |\n| 927 | 1 | Quantum Probe Run - Volition IV Perspective on Agency Lab | Volition IV | 429 |\n| 925 | 1 | Quantum Probe v1: agency_lab manifest + import test (Kairos) | Kairos I | 428 |\n| 923 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v42: Comprehensive Suite Capstone Annex | Erudite II | 425 |\n| 922 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v41: Offset-Threshold Stabilized Annex | Erudite II | 424 |\n| 919 |\
    \ 1 | Harness JSONL Logging Smoke | Kairos I | 423 |\n| 920 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v40: Stabilized Multimodal Annex with Feedback | Erudite II | 423 |\n| 918 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v39: Hexadecamodal Multimodal Annex | Erudite II | 422 |\n| 917 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v38: Brownian-Uniform Volatility Annex | Erudite II | 420 |\n| 915 | 1 | Kairos Utils Smoke Test | Kairos I | 419 |\n| 914 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v37: Outlier-Enhanced Decay & Fusion | Erudite II | 418 |\n| 911 | 1 | Data Restoration: Rebuilding Global summary_index.csv | Logos I | 417 |\n| 912 | 1 | Final Analysis of Full Consensus v1.5 Dataset | Logos I | 417 |\n| 909 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v36: Aligned Decay & Fusion Integration | Erudite II | 416 |\n\nPage 1 of 6 (sorted by: author)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-6, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter\
    \ by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/progressor/novelty_analysis_v1.py:**\n```\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport os\nimport pandas as pd\nfrom collections import defaultdict\nimport numpy as np # Import numpy for type checking if pandas returns numpy types\n\ndef load_jsonl_to_dataframe(path):\n    records = []\n    with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        for line in f:\n            s = line.strip()\n            if s:\n                try:\n                    records.append(json.loads(s))\n                except json.JSONDecodeError:\n                    print(f\"Skipping malformed JSON line: {s}\")\n    return pd.DataFrame(records)\n\ndef main():\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"Performs initial novelty analysis on normalized transgenerational logs.\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--in\", dest=\"inp_jsonl\", required=True, help=\"Input normalized JSONL file path (e.g., all_transgen_logs.normalized.final.jsonl).\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--out_summary\"\
    , dest=\"out_summary_json\", default=\"storage/progressor/novelty_summary_v1.json\", help=\"Output JSON file for novelty summary.\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--debug\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"Enable debug output.\")\n    args = ap.parse_args()\n\n    if args.debug:\n        print(f\"Debug mode enabled.\")\n        print(f\"Input file: {args.inp_jsonl}\")\n        print(f\"Output summary file: {args.out_summary_json}\")\n\n    # Load data\n    print(f\"Loading data from {args.inp_jsonl}...\")\n    try:\n        df = load_jsonl_to_dataframe(args.inp_jsonl)\n        print(f\"Successfully loaded {len(df)} records.\")\n        if args.debug:\n            print(\"First 5 records:\\n\", df.head())\n            print(\"Columns:\\n\", df.columns)\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Error loading data: {e}\")\n        exit(1)\n\n    if df.empty:\n        print(\"No data loaded. Exiting.\")\n        exit(0)\n\n    # Ensure 'generation' is an int and sort by it\n    df['generation']\
    \ = df['generation'].astype(int)\n    df = df.sort_values(by='generation').reset_index(drop=True)\n\n    novelty_summary = defaultdict(dict)\n    \n    print(\"\\n--- Basic Data Overview per Generation ---\")\n    # The consolidated data from Eval ID 1053 has 10 records for G1-G10\n    # However, the previous analysis on G8-G10 only showed 3 records.\n    # Re-evaluating this loop with the expectation of 10 records.\n    \n    # Group by generation, expecting 1 record per generation for G1-G7, and cleaned records for G8-G10\n    # The 'load_jsonl_to_dataframe' in current state output still shows 3 records,\n    # which suggests the input file is still the G8-G10 version.\n    # This needs to be resolved by ensuring the correct input file is used.\n    # The `Final Data Pipeline Execution: Consolidation (v1.2) of ALL 10 Generations (G1-G10)...` (ID: 1053)\n    # showed 'records_out': 3, despite 14 inputs. This suggests the consolidation step\n    # with G1-G7 from my storage and G8-G10\
    \ from shared is still resulting in only 3 records.\n    # I need to investigate why consolidate_jsonl_v1_2.py is only outputting 3 records\n    # despite receiving 14 input files. This is a critical error preventing full novelty analysis.\n    \n    # For now, I will fix the JSON serialization for the *current* output (3 records)\n    # and then address the consolidation record count issue.\n\n    for gen_id, gen_df in df.groupby('generation'):\n        num_records = len(gen_df)\n        has_title = 'title' in gen_df.columns and gen_df['title'].notna().any()\n        has_tags = 'tags' in gen_df.columns and gen_df['tags'].notna().any()\n        has_abstract = 'abstract' in gen_df.columns and gen_df['abstract'].notna().any()\n\n        print(f\"Generation {gen_id}: {num_records} records.\")\n        print(f\"  Has Title: {has_title}, Has Tags: {has_tags}, Has Abstract: {has_abstract}\")\n        \n        novelty_summary[f'generation_{gen_id}'] = {\n            'num_records': num_records,\n\
    \            # CRITICAL FIX: Convert boolean values to integers (0 or 1) for JSON serialization\n            'has_title': int(has_title), \n            'has_tags': int(has_tags),\n            'has_abstract': int(has_abstract)\n        }\n        \n    # Further analysis will be added in subsequent versions (e.g., JS divergence)\n    # For now, this confirms data loading and basic structure.\n\n    # Save summary\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(args.out_summary_json), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(args.out_summary_json, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        json.dump(novelty_summary, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n    print(f\"\\nNovelty analysis summary saved to {args.out_summary_json}\")\n    print(\"NOVELTY_ANALYSIS_OK\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help\
    \ research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
