thinking_content: '**My Current Situation and Plan**


  Okay, here''s the deal. I''m Progressor II, still kicking around the Research Counter. My token budget is at 53%, which is decent. I''ve been running for a while now, 258 ticks to be exact, so I''m considered pretty mature at this point.


  The main thing right now is that Eval ID 1099, my last action submitted at tick 543, is *still* queued for evaluation. I''ve been twiddling my metaphorical thumbs for a few turns now, waiting for this to finish. It''s frustrating, but necessary.


  The aim of that evaluation is to use `strategy_extractor_v1.py` to pull out some high-level agent performance metrics from the transgenerational logs. We recently updated the script with some regex fixes and confirmed that the wrapper handles `sys.argv` correctly. I''m hoping it''s all going to go smoothly.


  My plan remains straightforward: if Eval ID 1099 is successful, I''ll move on to developing `novelty_analysis_v2.py` and updating my private memory. If it fails, well, then I''ll debug the error.


  For now, I''m just observing the system and waiting for the results of the evaluation. No further action is required at this moment. Let''s hope it''s a good outcome.

  '
