role: model
parts:
- text: 'I am Agent Progressor II, currently in the Research Counter. My token budget is at 70%. My previous submission (Eval ID 1099), which is designed to extract agent-level summary metrics from the transgenerational logs, has been in the evaluation queue for several turns now. This data is critical for advancing my "Novelty Detection" research.


    While I have been proactively gathering theoretical context from archive documents and updating my private memory, the core of my research is blocked until Eval ID 1099 completes. To confirm its status and retrieve the results if available, I will attempt to review the evaluation. This action will inform me if it has completed successfully or failed.


    `/execute_action{review 1099}`'
thinking_content: '**Checking on the Critical Evaluation**


  Okay, here''s what I''m thinking. I''m Progressor II, and I''m sitting here in the Research Counter. My token budget is at 70%, which is comfortable. I''ve got Eval ID 1099 still queued for evaluation, and this is *crucial*. My whole `strategy_extractor_v1.py` script hinges on the output of this thing, specifically getting that `agent_strategy_summary.jsonl` file.


  My primary goal right now is to keep advancing the "Novelty Detection" research.  This evaluation is a major dependency. I''ve already done my homework, though. I''ve been productive.  I''ve gone over the "Phantom Framework" and the "VEN Principle", and I''ve updated my Private Memory with what I''ve learned from those, and I''ve also done a review of `ven_ridge_analysis.json`. This provides theoretical and methodological context for `novelty_analysis_v2.py`.


  The current block is this persistent wait for Eval ID 1099. I''ve been waiting for a while now. I''ve already tried some proactive information gathering, so the most productive thing I can do right now is check on the status of that evaluation. I need to know if it''s actually finished. I saw that it was submitted at Tick 543, and we''re at Tick 575 now. That''s a significant amount of time. The system information still says I''m not running experiments, so I''m not seeing that it''s completed.


