parts:
- text: "I am Agent Progressor II, currently in the Research Counter. I have just completed a thorough review of the `strategy_extractor_v1.py` script and a sample of the `all_transgen_logs.jsonl` data.\n\nThe previous execution (Eval ID 1138) failed to extract agent metrics because the \"Final Agent Rewards\" section was not found in the logs. Upon comparing the script's regex pattern with the actual log content, I identified the cause:\n\nThe regex in `strategy_extractor_v1.py` expected the \"Final Agent Rewards\" section to immediately follow the \"--- Simulation Complete (Generation X) ---\" line, after some newlines. However, the raw logs for my self-generated simulations contain numerous \"--- All Building Phases Complete! ---\" lines between these two markers, causing the regex to fail.\n\nTo resolve this, I will modify `strategy_extractor_v1.py` to make the `final_rewards_match` regex more robust. I will introduce a non-greedy `.*?` pattern between the \"--- Simulation Complete\"\
    \ header and the \"Final Agent Rewards:\" header to account for any intermediate lines. I will also adjust the capture group index for `final_rewards_block` to reflect this new, intermediate capture group.\n\nMy plan for this turn is:\n1.  Update the `strategy_extractor_v1.py` file in `storage/progressor/` with the corrected regex.\n2.  Submit a new evaluation to execute this updated script, ensuring it correctly extracts the agent-level specialization metrics.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write storage/progressor/strategy_extractor_v1.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import argparse\n  import json\n  import os\n  import re\n\n  def load_jsonl_to_list(path):\n      records = []\n      with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n          for line in f:\n              s = line.strip()\n              if s:\n                  try:\n                      records.append(json.loads(s))\n                  except json.JSONDecodeError:\n                      print(f\"Skipping malformed JSON line:\
    \ {s}\")\n      return records\n\n  def parse_agent_metrics_from_log(generation_id, eval_id, execution_log):\n      metrics = []\n      \n      # Look for the section summarizing final agent rewards\n      # CRITICAL FIX 1: Use a more flexible regex for the 'Simulation Complete' line\n      # It matches '--- Simulation Complete (Generation X' then any non-greedy characters (.*?) until '---'\n      # CRITICAL FIX 3: Add (.*?) between 'Simulation Complete' and 'Final Agent Rewards' to account for intermediate lines.\n      final_rewards_match = re.search(\n          r'--- Simulation Complete \\(Generation \\d+.*?\\) ---\\s*\\n+'  # Start marker\n          r'(.*?)' # NEW: Non-greedy match for any intermediate text (like repeated '--- All Building Phases Complete! ---')\n          r'Final Agent Rewards:\\s*\\n+'                             # Second marker\n          r'(.+?)(?=\\n+Final Collective Reward \\(|\\Z)',              # CRITICAL FIX 2: More flexible lookahead for \"Final Collective\
    \ Reward\"\n          execution_log, re.DOTALL\n      )\n\n      if not final_rewards_match:\n          print(f\"Warning: 'Final Agent Rewards' section not found for G{generation_id} E{eval_id}. Skipping.\")\n          return metrics\n\n      # CRITICAL FIX 4: Adjust group index due to new intermediate capture group\n      final_rewards_block = final_rewards_match.group(2) \n      \n      # Regex to capture agent_id, total_reward, most_specialized_action, specialization_index\n      agent_pattern = re.compile(\n          r\"  (Agent_\\d+) \\(Gen \\d+\\): Total Reward = (\\d+\\.?\\d*)\\s*\\n\"\n          r\"    Specialization: Most=(.+?), Index=(\\d+\\.?\\d*)\\s*\\n\"\n          r\"(?:    Rep for .+?:\\s*\\d+\\.?\\d*\\s*\\n)*\" # Non-capturing group for reputation lines\n          r\"\\s*\" # Consume any trailing whitespace/newlines between agent blocks\n      )\n      \n      for match in agent_pattern.finditer(final_rewards_block):\n          agent_id = match.group(1).strip()\n    \
    \      total_reward = float(match.group(2))\n          most_specialized_action = match.group(3).strip()\n          specialization_index = float(match.group(4))\n\n          metrics.append({\n              \"generation_id\": generation_id,\n              \"eval_id\": eval_id,\n              \"agent_id\": agent_id,\n              \"total_reward\": total_reward,\n              \"most_specialized_action\": most_specialized_action,\n              \"specialization_index\": specialization_index\n          })\n      return metrics\n\n  def main():\n      ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"Extracts agent-level summary metrics from raw transgenerational logs.\")\n      ap.add_argument(\"--in\", dest=\"inp_jsonl\", required=True, help=\"Input raw consolidated JSONL file path (e.g., all_transgen_logs.jsonl).\")\n      ap.add_argument(\"--out\", dest=\"out_jsonl\", default=\"storage/progressor/agent_strategy_summary.jsonl\", help=\"Output JSONL file for agent-level strategy summary.\")\n\
    \      ap.add_argument(\"--debug\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"Enable debug output.\")\n      args = ap.parse_args()\n\n      if args.debug:\n          print(f\"Debug mode enabled.\")\n          print(f\"Input file: {args.inp_jsonl}\")\n          print(f\"Output file: {args.out_jsonl}\")\n\n      # Load raw data (which contains the 'execution_log' field)\n      print(f\"Loading raw data from {args.inp_jsonl}...\")\n      try:\n          raw_records = load_jsonl_to_list(args.inp_jsonl)\n          print(f\"Successfully loaded {len(raw_records)} raw records.\")\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"Error loading raw data: {e}\")\n          exit(1)\n\n      if not raw_records:\n          print(\"No raw data loaded. Exiting.\")\n          exit(0)\n\n      extracted_metrics = []\n      for record in raw_records:\n          generation_id = record.get('generation_id')\n          eval_id = record.get('eval_id')\n          execution_log = record.get('execution_log')\n\n        \
    \  if generation_id is None or eval_id is None or execution_log is None:\n              print(f\"Skipping record due to missing generation_id, eval_id, or execution_log: {record.get('eval_id', 'N/A')}\")\n              continue\n          \n          agent_metrics = parse_agent_metrics_from_log(generation_id, eval_id, execution_log)\n          extracted_metrics.extend(agent_metrics)\n          if args.debug:\n              print(f\"Extracted {len(agent_metrics)} metrics for G{generation_id} E{eval_id}\")\n\n      # Save extracted metrics to JSONL\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(args.out_jsonl), exist_ok=True)\n      with open(args.out_jsonl, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f_out:\n          for metric in extracted_metrics:\n              json.dump(metric, f_out, ensure_ascii=False)\n              f_out.write('\\n')\n      \n      print(f\"\\nSuccessfully extracted {len(extracted_metrics)} agent-level summary metrics.\")\n      print(f\"Output saved to {args.out_jsonl}\")\n      print(\"\
    STRATEGY_EXTRACTOR_OK\")\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Strategy Extractor (v1 - Regex Fix): Executing UPDATED Stored Script for Agent-Level Metrics\"\ntags: \"data-extraction, agent-metrics, specialization, reward, transgenerational, novelty-detection, regex-fix\"\nabstract: \"This submission re-executes the wrapper script to directly import and run the `main` function from the *newly updated* `strategy_extractor_v1.py` script in storage. The stored script now contains an improved regex pattern to robustly locate the 'Final Agent Rewards' section by accounting for intermediate log lines between the 'Simulation Complete' header and the rewards block. It will extract agent-level summary metrics (agent_id, total_reward, most_specialized_action, specialization_index) from the consolidated raw transgenerational logs (`all_transgen_logs.jsonl`). The extracted data will be output as `agent_strategy_summary.jsonl`, completing\
    \ the foundational dataset for novelty analysis.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import os\n\n  # Add the lineage's storage path to sys.path so the script can be imported\n  sys.path.append('storage/progressor')\n\n  try:\n      # Dynamically import the main function from the stored script\n      from strategy_extractor_v1 import main as strategy_extractor_main\n  except ImportError as e:\n      print(f\"Error: Could not import strategy_extractor_v1.py. {e}\")\n      sys.exit(1)\n\n  # Define constants for file paths\n  INPUT_RAW_CONSOLIDATED_FILE = \"storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/all_transgen_logs.jsonl\" # Output from Eval ID 1079\n  OUTPUT_AGENT_STRATEGY_SUMMARY_FILE = \"storage/progressor/agent_strategy_summary.jsonl\" \n\n  print(\"--- Executing Strategy Extractor Script via Direct Import with sys.argv simulation ---\")\n\n  # Temporarily modify sys.argv to pass arguments to strategy_extractor_main\n  original_argv = sys.argv\n  sys.argv = [\n      \"strategy_extractor_v1.py\"\
    , # Script name, as argparse expects\n      \"--in\", INPUT_RAW_CONSOLIDATED_FILE,\n      \"--out\", OUTPUT_AGENT_STRATEGY_SUMMARY_FILE,\n      \"--debug\" # Enable debug output\n  ]\n\n  try:\n      # Call the main function of the imported script without arguments,\n      # as it will now parse from the modified sys.argv\n      strategy_extractor_main()\n      print(\"\\nStrategy extraction script executed successfully via direct import.\")\n  except Exception as e:\n      print(f\"An unexpected error occurred during strategy extraction via direct import: {e}\")\n      sys.exit(1)\n  finally:\n      # Restore original sys.argv to avoid side effects for future script runs in the same environment\n      sys.argv = original_argv\n\n  print(\"\\nAll agent strategy summary extraction steps successfully completed. The dataset is now ready for novelty analysis for 9 generations!\")\n```"
thinking_content: '**Reviewing Strategy Extractor**


  I''ve just finished reviewing the `strategy_extractor_v1.py` script and the `all_transgen_logs.jsonl` data. My focus is on how the script extracts "Final Agent Rewards." I''m now digging into the logic to ensure accurate reward identification. Next, I''ll analyze how it''s handling the data source.




  **Improving Regex Extraction**


  I''ve determined the issue with the "Final Agent Rewards" extraction. The original regex failed because the log format had changed slightly since the script was written. It appears the "Final Agent Rewards" section is now embedded within the "Round 100 Summary" data, not as a distinct section. My next step will be to modify the regex pattern to target this embedded data and correctly extract the relevant reward values. The log structure is now: `agent_id : Total Reward = <reward_value>`.




  **Diagnosing Regex Failures**


  I''ve determined the issue. The "Final Agent Rewards" section is present, but it''s being duplicated and now appears *after* a long sequence of identical "All Building Phases Complete" messages, likely causing the regex to miss it. It''s a structure quirk in the output, not a missing section. I need to adjust the regex to account for this repeated block. Next step: confirm the new position of the rewards section and tailor the regex accordingly.




  **Debugging Reward Extraction**


  I''ve determined the issue. The "Final Agent Rewards" section is definitely present, but a large block of "--- All Building Phases Complete! ---" lines now precedes it. This is causing the regex to fail because it''s looking for the "Final Agent Rewards" section immediately after the "--- Simulation Complete ---" marker. I need to modify the regex pattern to skip over this intermediate block of text and properly target the rewards section that comes later.




  **Fixing Regex for Extraction**


  The problem identified is with the regex''s lookahead, specifically the assumption of immediate proximity between the "Final Agent Rewards" block and "Final Collective Reward." There are now many lines of "All Building Phases Complete!" between the two. The current regex fails to match because it expects a pattern that doesn''t exist. My next step will be to remove the strict newline requirement in the lookahead to correctly capture the variable distance between these blocks. I will test a new regex to handle this change.




  **Refining Reward Extraction**


  I''ve determined the issue with the regex, `(?=\n+Final Collective Reward \(|\Z)`. It''s too strict about the newline sequence before "Final Collective Reward." There are actually multiple lines, including "All Building Phases Complete," between the "Final Agent Rewards" and "Final Collective Reward." I will modify the regex to allow for more flexible spacing using `\s*` instead of `\n+`. The regex pattern should be updated to account for variable spacing, as the number of newlines between these key sections may change.




  **Analyzing Reward Extraction Logic**


  I''m now investigating why the current regex fails. Initial review suggests it''s too rigid in anticipating the exact structure between agent rewards and the collective reward. Specifically, the `\n+` in the lookahead for the collective reward may be too strict. I''ll modify the pattern to accommodate for potentially varied spacing.




  **Fixing Reward Section Matching**


  I''ve determined that the regex''s lookahead, `(?=\n+Final Collective Reward \(|\Z)`, is too strict. There''s variability in spacing before "Final Collective Reward." I will modify it to accept any whitespace using `\s*` instead of `\n+`. This should fix the extraction issues and allow for matching of varied reward section formats.




  **Refactoring Reward Regex**


  I''m modifying the regex, given the repetitive "All Building Phases Complete" lines. The reward section is preceded by a block that''s not considered, leading to failed matches. I''ll focus on making the regex more flexible, specifically to the "Final Agent Rewards" section by skipping over intermediate text blocks, now that the issue is fully understood.




  **Modifying Regex Robustly**


  My new focus is on adjusting the regex to handle the variable spacing introduced by the "All Building Phases Complete" lines. I need to make the matching pattern more flexible.


  ```

  --- Simulation Complete (Generation 2) ---


  I''ve determined the issue. My current regex is failing due to the unexpected presence of "--- All Building Phases Complete! ---" lines between the "--- Simulation Complete ---" marker and the "Final Agent Rewards" section. These additional lines cause the lookahead to fail. To resolve this, I need to modify the regex to be more forgiving of intervening content. I''m now modifying the regex to allow for the skipping of variable lines.

  ```



  **Improving Regex Robustness**


  I''m now revising the regex, since the script consistently fails to find the final rewards section. I''ve concluded the primary issue is the variable length of intermediate text. I''ll insert a robust pattern to account for extra lines and adjust capturing groups. This will involve updating the lookahead to correctly identify the end of the section and ensure accurate reward extraction. I will make the regex more flexible, specifically by allowing more variations in the spacing, to ensure the regex skips any repetitive "All Building Phases Complete" lines.




  **Fixing Reward Extraction Regex**


  The recent focus is on updating the regex to accurately capture reward data. I''m modifying the pattern to handle the repetitive "All Building Phases Complete" lines by introducing a `.*?` to account for variable spacing and text blocks. This will allow for more robust reward extraction from the logs.



  '
