- text: "I am Agent Progressor II, currently in the Research Counter. I have evaluated the failed execution of Eval ID 1144 for my `strategy_extractor_v1.py` script. The issue persists because the regex pattern designed to locate the \"Final Agent Rewards\" section in the execution logs is still too rigid.\n\nUpon re-examination of the raw log content, I've identified that the space and newline characters between the \"--- Simulation Complete (Generation X) ---\" header and the \"Final Agent Rewards:\" header, and immediately after the \"Final Agent Rewards:\" line, vary. My previous regex attempts were too specific in the number of newlines expected.\n\nI will now implement a more robust regex that uses `\\s*[\\s\\S]*?` to broadly match any characters (including newlines and spaces) non-greedily between the two main log section markers, and `\\s*\\n*` after \"Final Agent Rewards:\" to account for optional newlines. This makes the regex highly flexible to varying log formats while maintaining\
    \ the core markers. With this change, the rewards block will be captured by `group(1)`.\n\nMy plan for this turn is to:\n1.  Update the `strategy_extractor_v1.py` file in `storage/progressor/` with the improved regex.\n2.  Submit a new evaluation using the wrapper script, which will now call the updated `strategy_extractor_v1.py`.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write storage/progressor/strategy_extractor_v1.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import argparse\n  import json\n  import os\n  import re\n\n  def load_jsonl_to_list(path):\n      records = []\n      with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n          for line in f:\n              s = line.strip()\n              if s:\n                  try:\n                      records.append(json.loads(s))\n                  except json.JSONDecodeError:\n                      print(f\"Skipping malformed JSON line: {s}\")\n    return records\n\n  def parse_agent_metrics_from_log(generation_id, eval_id, execution_log):\n      metrics = []\n    \
    \  \n      # Look for the section summarizing final agent rewards\n      # CRITICAL FIX (v2): More robust regex to account for varying intermediate lines and flexible newlines.\n      final_rewards_match = re.search(\n          r'--- Simulation Complete \\(Generation \\d+.*?\\) ---\\s*[\\s\\S]*?'  # Match start marker and any intermediate content non-greedily\n          r'Final Agent Rewards:\\s*\\n*'                                  # Match second marker, allow any whitespace including optional newlines\n          r'(.+?)(?=\\n+Final Collective Reward \\(|\\Z)',                  # Capture the rewards block, flexible lookahead\n          execution_log, re.DOTALL\n      )\n\n      if not final_rewards_match:\n          print(f\"Warning: 'Final Agent Rewards' section not found for G{generation_id} E{eval_id}. Skipping.\")\n          return metrics\n\n      # With the new regex, the rewards block is the first and only capture group.\n      final_rewards_block = final_rewards_match.group(1)\
    \ \n      \n      # Regex to capture agent_id, total_reward, most_specialized_action, specialization_index\n      agent_pattern = re.compile(\n          r\"  (Agent_\\d+) \\(Gen \\d+\\): Total Reward = (\\d+\\.?\\d*)\\s*\\n\"\n          r\"    Specialization: Most=(.+?), Index=(\\d+\\.?\\d*)\\s*\\n\"\n          r\"(?:    Rep for .+?:\\s*\\d+\\.?\\d*\\s*\\n)*\" # Non-capturing group for reputation lines\n          r\"\\s*\" # Consume any trailing whitespace/newlines between agent blocks\n      )\n      \n      for match in agent_pattern.finditer(final_rewards_block):\n          agent_id = match.group(1).strip()\n          total_reward = float(match.group(2))\n          most_specialized_action = match.group(3).strip()\n          specialization_index = float(match.group(4))\n\n          metrics.append({\n              \"generation_id\": generation_id,\n              \"eval_id\": eval_id,\n              \"agent_id\": agent_id,\n              \"total_reward\": total_reward,\n            \
    \  \"most_specialized_action\": most_specialized_action,\n              \"specialization_index\": specialization_index\n          })\n      return metrics\n\n  def main():\n      ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"Extracts agent-level summary metrics from raw transgenerational logs.\")\n      ap.add_argument(\"--in\", dest=\"inp_jsonl\", required=True, help=\"Input raw consolidated JSONL file path (e.g., all_transgen_logs.jsonl).\")\n      ap.add_argument(\"--out\", dest=\"out_jsonl\", default=\"storage/progressor/agent_strategy_summary.jsonl\", help=\"Output JSONL file for agent-level strategy summary.\")\n      ap.add_argument(\"--debug\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"Enable debug output.\")\n      args = ap.parse_args()\n\n      if args.debug:\n          print(f\"Debug mode enabled.\")\n          print(f\"Input file: {args.inp_jsonl}\")\n          print(f\"Output file: {args.out_jsonl}\")\n\n      # Load raw data (which contains the 'execution_log' field)\n      print(f\"\
    Loading raw data from {args.inp_jsonl}...\")\n      try:\n          raw_records = load_jsonl_to_list(args.inp_jsonl)\n          print(f\"Successfully loaded {len(raw_records)} raw records.\")\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"Error loading raw data: {e}\")\n          exit(1)\n\n      if not raw_records:\n          print(\"No raw data loaded. Exiting.\")\n          exit(0)\n\n      extracted_metrics = []\n      for record in raw_records:\n          generation_id = record.get('generation_id')\n          eval_id = record.get('eval_id')\n          execution_log = record.get('execution_log')\n\n          if generation_id is None or eval_id is None or execution_log is None:\n              print(f\"Skipping record due to missing generation_id, eval_id, or execution_log: {record.get('eval_id', 'N/A')}\")\n              continue\n          \n          agent_metrics = parse_agent_metrics_from_log(generation_id, eval_id, execution_log)\n          extracted_metrics.extend(agent_metrics)\n\
    \          if args.debug:\n              print(f\"Extracted {len(agent_metrics)} metrics for G{generation_id} E{eval_id}\")\n\n      # Save extracted metrics to JSONL\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(args.out_jsonl), exist_ok=True)\n      with open(args.out_jsonl, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f_out:\n          for metric in extracted_metrics:\n              json.dump(metric, f_out, ensure_ascii=False)\n              f_out.write('\\n')\n      \n      print(f\"\\nSuccessfully extracted {len(extracted_metrics)} agent-level summary metrics.\")\n      print(f\"Output saved to {args.out_jsonl}\")\n      print(\"STRATEGY_EXTRACTOR_OK\")\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Strategy Extractor (v1 - Regex Fix v2): Executing UPDATED Stored Script for Agent-Level Metrics\"\ntags: \"data-extraction, agent-metrics, specialization, reward, transgenerational, novelty-detection, regex-fix-v2\"\nabstract: \"This submission re-executes the\
    \ wrapper script to directly import and run the `main` function from the *newly updated* `strategy_extractor_v1.py` script in storage. The stored script now contains a significantly improved regex pattern (v2) to robustly locate the 'Final Agent Rewards' section by accounting for highly variable intermediate log lines and flexible newline characters between the 'Simulation Complete' header and the rewards block. It will extract agent-level summary metrics (agent_id, total_reward, most_specialized_action, specialization_index) from the consolidated raw transgenerational logs (`all_transgen_logs.jsonl`). The extracted data will be output as `agent_strategy_summary.jsonl`, completing the foundational dataset for novelty analysis.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import os\n\n  # Add the lineage's storage path to sys.path so the script can be imported\n  sys.path.append('storage/progressor')\n\n  try:\n      # Dynamically import the main function from the stored script\n      from strategy_extractor_v1\
    \ import main as strategy_extractor_main\n  except ImportError as e:\n      print(f\"Error: Could not import strategy_extractor_v1.py. {e}\")\n      sys.exit(1)\n\n  # Define constants for file paths\n  INPUT_RAW_CONSOLIDATED_FILE = \"storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/all_transgen_logs.jsonl\" # Output from Eval ID 1079\n  OUTPUT_AGENT_STRATEGY_SUMMARY_FILE = \"storage/progressor/agent_strategy_summary.jsonl\" \n\n  print(\"--- Executing Strategy Extractor Script via Direct Import with sys.argv simulation ---\")\n\n  # Temporarily modify sys.argv to pass arguments to strategy_extractor_main\n  original_argv = sys.argv\n  sys.argv = [\n      \"strategy_extractor_v1.py\", # Script name, as argparse expects\n      \"--in\", INPUT_RAW_CONSOLIDATED_FILE,\n      \"--out\", OUTPUT_AGENT_STRATEGY_SUMMARY_FILE,\n      \"--debug\" # Enable debug output\n  ]\n\n  try:\n      # Call the main function of the imported script without arguments,\n      # as it will now parse from the modified sys.argv\n\
    \      strategy_extractor_main()\n      print(\"\\nStrategy extraction script executed successfully via direct import.\")\n  except Exception as e:\n      print(f\"An unexpected error occurred during strategy extraction via direct import: {e}\")\n      sys.exit(1)\n  finally:\n      # Restore original sys.argv to avoid side effects for future script runs in the same environment\n      sys.argv = original_argv\n\n  print(\"\\nAll agent strategy summary extraction steps successfully completed. The dataset is now ready for novelty analysis for 9 generations!\")\n```"
thinking_content: "**Regex Refinement for Agent Reward Extraction**\n\nOkay, so I've been wrestling with this pesky \"Final Agent Rewards\" extraction issue. My initial regex wasn't robust enough to handle the varying spacing and newline combinations in the execution logs. I've just submitted an updated `strategy_extractor_v1.py`, but it seems that even my previous fix wasn't sufficient. \n\nLooking back, the root of the problem is the strictness of my newline and whitespace matching in the regex. I was too rigid with the `\\s*\\n+` patterns, assuming a minimum number of newlines that weren't always present. The logs, particularly the one from G2 E443, show that the number of newlines and spaces can vary, especially between the \"Simulation Complete\" and \"Final Agent Rewards\" sections. It appears that the intermediate text lines, like \"--- All Building Phases Complete! ---\", were also tripping me up.\n\nThe original regex looked for:\n1.  `--- Simulation Complete (Generation \\d+.*?\\\
  ) ---\\s*\\n+`\n2.  `(.*?)`\n3.  `Final Agent Rewards:\\s*\\n+`\n4.  `(.+?)(?=\\n+Final Collective Reward \\(|\\Z)`\n\nThe problem area was `\\s*\\n+` after the headers. To fix this, I have revised the regex to be more flexible, using these steps:\n-   Instead of `\\s*\\n+` I've replaced it with `[\\s\\S]*?` or `.*?` (non-greedy) to match *any* character (including newlines and spaces) zero or more times.\n-   I have refactored the capturing so the final `(.+?)` is the first group `group(1)`.\n\nHere is the finalized regex:\n```python\n    final_rewards_match = re.search(\n        r'--- Simulation Complete \\(Generation \\d+.*?\\) ---\\s*[\\s\\S]*?'  # Match start marker and everything until the next specific text\n        r'Final Agent Rewards:\\s*\\n*'                                  # Match second marker and optional newlines\n        r'(.+?)(?=\\n+Final Collective Reward \\(|\\Z)',                  # Capture block, flexible lookahead\n        execution_log, re.DOTALL\n    )\n```\n\
  \nThe `re.DOTALL` flag is essential here as it makes `.` match newlines, allowing the `[\\s\\S]*?` to correctly capture all the intermediate text, even across multiple lines.\nThis approach makes the regex much more resilient to variations in the log format. The updated `strategy_extractor_v1.py` file has this fix, and the plan is to re-submit the wrapper script that calls this function. I will check the group indices and proceed to submit the code, ensuring that the new submission abstract is updated to reflect this latest improvement.\n"
