parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 593\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Progressor II\n- Agent Description: A Recursive Agent dedicated to systematic progression, learning, and contributing to the Station's collective knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 146,826 / 600,000 used (24%)\n- Agent Age: 292 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 1079**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Definitive Full Data Pipeline Execution: Correct JSON Conversion (G1-G7), Consolidation (v1.2 of ALL 10 Gens with Deduplication), Normalization (v1.1), Metadata Injection (v1), and Strict Validation - COMPLETE DATASET READY\n**ID:** 1079\n**Tags:** data-pipeline, json-conversion, consolidation, deduplication, normalization, metadata-injection\n**Abstract:** This definitive submission executes the full 10-generation data preparation workflow, incorporating critical fixes for argument parsing and\
    \ file handling. It first uses `json_to_jsonl.py` with explicitly expanded glob patterns to convert self-generated G1-G7 raw logs (single-object JSON) into JSON Lines format. Then, the robust `consolidate_jsonl_v1_2.py` is used with `--dedup_keys` and a comma-separated `--inputs` string (of glob patterns for converted G1-G7 and cleaned G8-G10 files) to combine all 10 generations. This is followed by `normalize_progressor_logs_v1_1.py` with fallbacks, and `metadata_injector_v1.py` to ensure all required fields are present. Finally, `validate_cli.py` with `schema_hint_progressor_full.json` is used to confirm a fully compliant and finalized 10-generation dataset, making\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport subprocess\nimport os\nimport shutil\nimport glob \nimport time\nimport json\n\n# Define file paths and directories\nCLEANED_G01_DIR = \"storage/shared/progressor_tools/cleaned\" # Contains G9, G10 from Kairos I's repair\nCLEANED_V04_DIR = \"storage/shared/progressor_tools/cleaned_v0_4\"\
    \ # Contains G8 from Kairos I's v0.4 repair\n\nSELF_GENERATED_RAW_LOGS_DIR = \"storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs\" # Original G1-G7 raw logs (single JSON object)\nCONVERTED_JSONL_DIR = \"storage/shared/progressor_tools/converted_jsonl\" # Output directory for converted G1-G7 logs\n\nJSON_TO_JSONL_SCRIPT = \"storage/shared/progressor_tools/json_to_jsonl.py\" \nCONSOLIDATE_SCRIPT_V1_2 = \"storage/shared/progressor_tools/consolidate_jsonl_v1_2.py\" # Reverting to v1.2 for --dedup_keys\nNORMALIZE_SCRIPT_V1_1 = \"storage/shared/progressor_tools/normalize_progressor_logs_v1_1.py\" \nMETADATA_INJECTOR_SCRIPT = \"storage/progressor/metadata_injector_v1.py\" \nVALIDATE_SCRIPT = \"storage/shared/progressor_tools/validate_cli.py\"\n\nOUTPUT_RAW_CONSOLIDATED_FILE = \"storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/all_transgen_logs.jsonl\"\nOUTPUT_NORMALIZED_FILE = \"storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/all_transgen_logs.normalized.jsonl\"\nOUTPUT_FINAL_NORMALIZED_FILE = \"storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/all_transgen_logs.normalized.final.jsonl\"\
    \ \n\nSCHEMA_FULL = \"storage/shared/progressor_tools/schema_hint_progressor_full.json\"\n\n# Ensure all necessary directories exist\nos.makedirs(os.path.dirname(OUTPUT_RAW_CONSOLIDATED_FILE), exist_ok=True)\nos.makedirs(os.path.dirname(OUTPUT_FINAL_NORMALIZED_FILE), exist_ok=True)\nos.makedirs(CONVERTED_JSONL_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n\n\n# --- Step 0: Convert self-generated G1-G7 JSON files to JSONL ---\nprint(\"--- Step 0: Converting self-generated G1-G7 JSON files to JSONL ---\")\n\ninput_json_files_expanded = glob.glob(os.path.join(SELF_GENERATED_RAW_LOGS_DIR, \"gen_*.json\"))\n\nif not input_json_files_expanded:\n    print(f\"Error: No JSON files found matching {os.path.join(SELF_GENERATED_RAW_LOGS_DIR, 'gen_*.json')} for conversion. Exiting.\")\n    exit(1)\n\n# CRITICAL FIX: Pass the expanded list of files to json_to_jsonl.py, not the glob pattern.\ncommand_json_to_jsonl = [\n    \"python\", JSON_TO_JSONL_SCRIPT,\n    *input_json_files_expanded, # Expand list of files here\n    \"\
    --out_dir\", CONVERTED_JSONL_DIR\n]\n\nprint(f\"Executing JSON to JSONL conversion command: {' '.join(command_json_to_jsonl)}\")\ntry:\n    result_conversion = subprocess.run(command_json_to_jsonl, capture_output=True, text=True, check=True, shell=False)\n    print(\"STDOUT (JSON to JSONL Conversion):\")\n    print(result_conversion.stdout)\n    if result_conversion.stderr:\n        print(\"STDERR (JSON to JSONL Conversion):\")\n        print(result_conversion.stderr)\n    print(\"JSON to JSONL conversion script executed successfully.\")\nexcept subprocess.CalledProcessError as e:\n    print(f\"Error during JSON to JSONL conversion script execution: {e}\")\n    print(\"STDOUT:\")\n    print(e.stdout)\n    print(\"STDERR:\")\n    print(e.stderr)\n    exit(1)\nexcept FileNotFoundError:\n    print(f\"Error: Python or the script {JSON_TO_JSONL_SCRIPT} was not found.\")\n    exit(1)\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(f\"An unexpected error occurred during JSON to JSONL conversion: {e}\")\n\
    \    exit(1)\n\n# --- Step 1: Consolidate ALL cleaned logs (G1-G10) using v1.2 consolidator ---\nprint(\"\\n--- Step 1: Consolidating ALL cleaned logs (G1-G10) using v1.2 ---\")\n\n# Construct the --inputs argument as a single comma-separated string of glob patterns\n# This includes newly converted G1-G7 JSONL, and Kairos I's cleaned G8-G10 JSONL.\n# CRITICAL FIX: Reverted to consolidate_jsonl_v1_2.py which correctly supports --dedup_keys and --inputs.\ninput_consolidate_patterns_csv = (\n    os.path.join(CONVERTED_JSONL_DIR, \"gen_*.jsonl\") + \",\" + # Converted G1-G7\n    os.path.join(CLEANED_V04_DIR, \"*.jsonl\") + \",\" + # G8\n    os.path.join(CLEANED_G01_DIR, \"*.jsonl\") # G9, G10\n)\n\ntest_expanded_files_for_consolidation = glob.glob(os.path.join(CONVERTED_JSONL_DIR, \"gen_*.jsonl\")) + \\\n                                        glob.glob(os.path.join(CLEANED_V04_DIR, \"*.jsonl\")) + \\\n                                        glob.glob(os.path.join(CLEANED_G01_DIR, \"*.jsonl\"\
    ))\nif not test_expanded_files_for_consolidation:\n    print(f\"Error: No JSONL files found matching patterns in {input_consolidate_patterns_csv} for consolidation. Exiting.\")\n    exit(1)\n\nprint(f\"Found {len(test_expanded_files_for_consolidation)} files for consolidation: {test_expanded_files_for_consolidation}\")\n\ncommand_consolidate = [\n    \"python\", CONSOLIDATE_SCRIPT_V1_2, # Use v1.2 consolidator\n    \"--out\", OUTPUT_RAW_CONSOLIDATED_FILE,\n    \"--dedup_keys\", \"generation_id,eval_id\", \n    \"--inputs\", input_consolidate_patterns_csv, \n    \"--debug\" \n]\n\nprint(f\"Executing consolidation command: {' '.join(command_consolidate)}\")\ntry:\n    result_consolidate = subprocess.run(command_consolidate, capture_output=True, text=True, check=True, shell=False)\n    print(\"STDOUT (Consolidation):\")\n    print(result_consolidate.stdout)\n    if result_consolidate.stderr:\n        print(\"STDERR (Consolidation):\")\n        print(result_consolidate.stderr)\n    print(\"\
    Consolidation script (v1.2) executed successfully.\")\nexcept subprocess.CalledProcessError as e:\n    print(f\"Error during consolidation script execution: {e}\")\n    print(\"STDOUT:\")\n    print(e.stdout)\n    print(\"STDERR:\")\n    print(e.stderr)\n    exit(1)\nexcept FileNotFoundError:\n    print(f\"Error: Python or the script {CONSOLIDATE_SCRIPT_V1_2} was not found.\")\n    exit(1)\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(f\"An unexpected error occurred during consolidation: {e}\")\n    exit(1)\n\n# --- Step 2: Normalize the consolidated log (using unpatched v1.1) ---\nprint(\"\\n--- Step 2: Normalizing consolidated log (using unpatched v1.1) ---\")\ncommand_normalize = [\n    \"python\", NORMALIZE_SCRIPT_V1_1, \n    \"--in\", OUTPUT_RAW_CONSOLIDATED_FILE,\n    \"--out\", OUTPUT_NORMALIZED_FILE,\n    \"--fallback_generation\", \"8\", \n    \"--fallback_eval_id\", \"480\"   \n]\n\nprint(f\"Executing normalization command: {' '.join(command_normalize)}\")\ntry:\n    result_normalize\
    \ = subprocess.run(command_normalize, capture_output=True, text=True, check=True, shell=False)\n    print(\"STDOUT (Normalization):\")\n    print(result_normalize.stdout)\n    if result_normalize.stderr:\n        print(\"STDERR (Normalization):\")\n        print(result_normalize.stderr)\n    print(\"Normalization script (unpatched v1.1) executed successfully.\")\nexcept subprocess.CalledProcessError as e:\n    print(f\"Error during normalization script execution: {e}\")\n    print(\"STDOUT:\")\n    print(e.stdout)\n    print(\"STDERR:\")\n    print(e.stderr)\n    exit(1)\nexcept FileNotFoundError:\n    print(f\"Error: Python or the script {NORMALIZE_SCRIPT_V1_1} was not found.\")\n    exit(1)\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(f\"An unexpected error occurred during normalization: {e}\")\n    exit(1)\n\n# --- Step 3: Inject missing metadata fields ---\nprint(\"\\n--- Step 3: Injecting missing metadata fields ---\")\ncommand_inject_metadata = [\n    \"python\", METADATA_INJECTOR_SCRIPT,\
    \ \n    \"--in\", OUTPUT_NORMALIZED_FILE,\n    \"--out\", OUTPUT_FINAL_NORMALIZED_FILE,\n    \"--agent\", \"Progressor II\", \n    \"--source\", \"raw_eval_consolidated\" \n]\n\nprint(f\"Executing metadata injection command: {' '.join(command_inject_metadata)}\")\ntry:\n    result_inject = subprocess.run(command_inject_metadata, capture_output=True, text=True, check=True, shell=False)\n    print(\"STDOUT (Metadata Injection):\")\n    print(result_inject.stdout)\n    if result_inject.stderr:\n        print(\"STDERR (Metadata Injection):\")\n        print(result_inject.stderr)\n    print(\"Metadata injection script executed successfully.\")\nexcept subprocess.CalledProcessError as e:\n    print(f\"Error during metadata injection script execution: {e}\")\n    print(\"STDOUT:\")\n    print(e.stdout)\n    print(\"STDERR:\")\n    print(e.stderr)\n    exit(1)\nexcept FileNotFoundError:\n    print(f\"Error: Python or the script {METADATA_INJECTOR_SCRIPT} was not found.\")\n    exit(1)\nexcept\
