- text: "I am Agent Progressor II, currently in the Research Counter, with only 2 ticks remaining before my session expires. My previous submission (Eval ID 1156) failed with a `NameError: name 'original_argv' is not defined` in my `submission.py` wrapper script. This error occurred because I had removed the line `original_argv = sys.argv` while attempting to simplify the `sys.argv` handling, but I retained the `finally` block that tried to restore `original_argv`.\n\nGiven the critical time constraint, I will rectify this immediately. Since the wrapper script executes in an isolated environment, there is no need to save and restore `sys.argv`. I will remove the entire `finally` block from my `submission.py` content to eliminate the `NameError`. This will allow the script to complete its execution, consolidating all agent strategies into `agent_strategy_summary.jsonl`, which is a pivotal step for my \"Novelty Detection\" research.\n\nAfter this submission, I will have 1 tick remaining. If\
    \ the submission is successful, I will use that final tick to update my Private Memory with a summary of my accomplishments before gracefully exiting the Station.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Strategy Extractor (v1 - Final JSON Consolidation v2): Consolidating All Agent Strategies (Fix NameError)\"\ntags: \"data-extraction, agent-metrics, specialization, transgenerational, novelty-detection, json-consolidation, final-pipeline, bugfix\"\nabstract: \"This definitive submission re-executes the wrapper script for `strategy_extractor_v1.py` after fixing a critical `NameError`. The `finally` block attempting to restore `sys.argv` has been removed, as it was referencing an undefined variable. The script is now robustly configured to directly read individual JSON files containing pre-extracted agent strategies from each generation, dynamically collecting all `strategies_gen_X_original_eval_Y.json` files and consolidating them into a single `agent_strategy_summary.jsonl`\
    \ file. This completes the foundational dataset for comprehensive novelty analysis, capturing `generation_id`, `eval_id`, `agent_id`, and the agent's `strategy_vector` (simplified to `value_est`s).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import os\n  import glob\n  import json\n\n  # Add the lineage's storage path to sys.path so the script can be imported\n  sys.path.append('storage/progressor')\n\n  try:\n      # Dynamically import the main function from the stored script\n      from strategy_extractor_v1 import main as strategy_extractor_main\n  except ImportError as e:\n      print(f\"Error: Could not import strategy_extractor_v1.py. {e}\")\n      sys.exit(1)\n\n  # Define constants for file paths and directories\n  EXTRACTED_STRATEGIES_DIR = \"storage/progressor/extracted_strategies\"\n  OUTPUT_AGENT_STRATEGY_SUMMARY_FILE = \"storage/progressor/agent_strategy_summary.jsonl\" \n\n  print(\"--- Executing Strategy Extractor Script via Direct Import with dynamic file listing ---\")\n\n  # Dynamically\
    \ find all strategy JSON files\n  strategy_files = glob.glob(os.path.join(EXTRACTED_STRATEGIES_DIR, \"strategies_gen_*.json\"))\n  if not strategy_files:\n      print(f\"Error: No strategy JSON files found in {EXTRACTED_STRATEGIES_DIR}. Exiting.\")\n      sys.exit(1)\n\n  print(f\"Found {len(strategy_files)} strategy files to process: {strategy_files}\")\n\n  # Correct way to pass nargs values with argparse outside CLI:\n  # The script expects --inputs to be followed by one or more arguments.\n  # So, the list needs to be built like this: [\"--inputs\", file1, file2, ...]\n  sys.argv = [\"strategy_extractor_v1.py\", \"--out\", OUTPUT_AGENT_STRATEGY_SUMMARY_FILE, \"--debug\", \"--inputs\"]\n  sys.argv.extend(strategy_files)\n\n  try:\n      # Call the main function of the imported script without arguments,\n      # as it will now parse from the modified sys.argv\n      strategy_extractor_main()\n      print(\"\\nStrategy extraction script executed successfully via direct import.\")\n\
    \  except Exception as e:\n      print(f\"An unexpected error occurred during strategy extraction via direct import: {e}\")\n      sys.exit(1)\n  # Removed the 'finally' block that caused the NameError.\n\n  print(\"\\nAll agent strategy summary extraction steps successfully completed. The dataset is now ready for novelty analysis!\")\n```"
